翻译:Flower一休 千欲 蓝岸 wendychen11 13711 Kim
校对:微微  协调:潇妹纸</b><b></b>

01:40.510 --> 01:43.260
<b>最新消息 次贷市场开始分崩离析</b><b>
The new story, the mortgage meltdown.</b>

01:43.350 --> 01:45.770
<b>由于次贷危机的发生 今天上午的最新数字表明</b><b>
This morning in the mortgage meltdown, new numbers showing</b>

01:45.850 --> 01:48.770
<b>失去住所的美国人数又创新高</b><b>
that a record number of Americans are losing their homes.</b>

01:48.850 --> 01:52.440
<b>在过去几个月的时间里 美国有70多家从事次贷业务的公司纷纷倒闭</b><b>
More than 70 mortgage companies have failed in the last few months in America,</b>

01:52.520 --> 01:56.860
<b>而现在贝尔斯登 以及大银行等大型企业</b><b>
and now the biggest of the big companies, the Bear Stearns, the big banks,</b>

01:56.990 --> 01:58.570
<b>要开始承担这一后果了</b><b>
are caught holding the bag.</b>

02:01.830 --> 02:05.200
<b>贝尔斯登 这家国内排名第五的投资银行</b><b>
The fifth largest investment bank in the country, Bear Stearns,</b>

02:05.290 --> 02:08.830
<b>以每股2美金的股价出售给了摩根大通银行</b><b>
is being sold for just $2 a share to JPMorgan.</b>

02:08.920 --> 02:12.130
<b>这宗交易是在政府的协助下进行的 目的是为了保全</b><b>
It's being assisted by the government, which is stepping in to guarantee</b>

02:12.210 --> 02:16.760
<b>贝尔斯登帐下的300亿美金的不良房地产资产</b><b>
some $30 billion in Bear's toxic real estate assets.</b>

02:19.380 --> 02:23.970
<b>你一定能想象得出来 汉克·保尔森被布什总统任命为财政部长的时候</b><b>
You've got to imagine that Hank Paulson didn't think he signed up for this</b>

02:24.060 --> 02:27.600
<b>不会想到有一天会去签署这样一份文件</b><b>
when President Bush picked him to become Treasury Secretary.</b>

02:27.980 --> 02:31.900
<b>现在汉克·保尔森可能不得不取消一些撤销管制的规定</b><b>
Hank Paulson may now have to undo some of the deregulation measures</b>

02:31.980 --> 02:35.860
<b>而这些措施恰恰是在他主管高盛集团时与华尔街上的同行们一直努力倡导的</b><b>
that he and his peers on Wall Street pushed through when he ran Goldman.</b>

02:37.820 --> 02:40.820
<b>汉克·保尔森财长今天上午对马特·劳尔说</b><b>
Treasury Secretary Hank Paulson telling Matt Lauer this morning,</b>

02:40.910 --> 02:44.620
<b>"我们已经克服了一切困难 我对我们的市场充满信心</b><b>
"We're all over it. I've got great confidence in our markets.</b>

02:44.700 --> 02:46.290
<b>它们是富有弹性和可塑性的"</b><b>
They're resilient. They're flexible."</b>

02:46.370 --> 02:51.080
<b>阿里 事实上贝尔斯登的收购事件只是掀开了冰山一角</b><b>
Ali, the truth is that Bear Stearns is only a very small fraction of this story.</b>

02:51.790 --> 02:55.630
<b>我们的经济很可能会大幅衰退</b><b>
Our economy could face far worse than a recession.</b>

02:58.590 --> 03:01.800
<b>受贝尔斯登倒闭的影响 雷曼兄弟忙于</b><b>
In the wake of Bear's collapse, Lehman Brothers is scrambling</b>

03:01.930 --> 03:06.180
<b>说服投资者相信 次贷危机不会对雷曼兄弟的资产造成太大影响</b><b>
to reassure investors about the impact of the mortgage crisis on its own assets.</b>

03:06.270 --> 03:09.020
<b>今天上午雷曼兄弟的保证人遭受了一系列的压力</b><b>
Insurers of the firm under a great deal of pressure this morning.</b>

03:09.100 --> 03:11.850
<b>迪克·富尔德 在雷曼工作了39年</b><b>
Dick Fuld, a 39-year veteran of Lehman</b>

03:11.940 --> 03:15.440
<b>并且是华尔街上大型投资银行中任职最久的首席执行官</b><b>
and the longest-running CEO of a major investment bank on Wall Street,</b>

03:15.520 --> 03:18.900
<b>曾多次让公司在危机中起死回生</b><b>
has pulled the firm back from the brink during other crises,</b>

03:19.440 --> 03:24.660
<b>理查德·福尔德</b>

03:19.440 --> 03:24.660
<b>雷曼兄弟主席兼首席执行官</b>

03:19.440 --> 03:21.660
<b>但是今天 我第一次听到了</b><b>
but today, for the first time that I'm hearing it,</b>

03:21.660 --> 03:24.660
<b>投资者们对他的领导能力的质疑声</b><b>
investors are questioning his leadership.</b>

03:24.740 --> 03:26.030
<b>- 混蛋  - 投资者们</b><b>
- Motherfucker.  - One key question</b>

03:26.120 --> 03:27.740
<b>对雷曼兄弟最关注的一个问题就是</b><b>
investors have for Lehman Brothers,</b>

03:27.830 --> 03:30.830
<b>"这家投资银行的盈利能力到底如何?"</b><b>
"What's the true earnings power of this investment bank's business?"</b>

03:32.560 --> 03:37.000
<b>乔·格雷戈里</b>

03:32.560 --> 03:37.000
<b>雷曼兄弟总裁兼首席运营官</b>

03:39.460 --> 03:41.380
<b>- 嘿  - 赶紧到我这儿来</b><b>
- Hey.  - Get up here.</b>

03:41.470 --> 03:43.300
<b>我们得去搬救兵了</b><b>
We gotta start stacking sand bags.</b>

03:43.470 --> 03:44.590
<b>你在说什么啊?</b><b>
What are you talking about?</b>

03:44.680 --> 03:49.770
<b>我们的股价暴跌了21% 从市价上看 我个人就损失了9000万</b><b>
We're down 21%. On paper, I just lost $90 million, personally.</b>

03:51.350 --> 03:53.690
<b>随着投资者不断抛售雷曼兄弟的股票</b><b>
With investors pummeling Lehman shares,</b>

03:53.770 --> 03:55.440
<b>今天上午最大的一个疑问就是</b><b>
the big question this morning is,</b>

03:55.520 --> 03:57.520
<b>"富尔德还有何退路?"</b><b>
"What options does Fuld have?"</b>

03:57.610 --> 03:59.940
<b>截至目前 他还没能够筹措到新的投资</b><b>
So far, he has failed to raise new capital</b>

04:00.030 --> 04:02.780
<b>而事实上他的竞争对手们已经拿到了</b><b>
while virtually all of his rivals have already done so.</b>

04:01.030 --> 04:04.780
<b>亨利·保尔森</b>

04:01.030 --> 04:04.780
<b>财政部长</b>

04:01.030 --> 04:04.780
<b>高盛前董事会主席兼首席执行官</b>

04:02.990 --> 04:05.160
<b>现在 对冲基金经理戴维·爱因霍恩</b><b>
And now, hedge fund manager David Einhorn</b>

04:05.160 --> 04:07.330
<b>已经在公开质疑公布数字的准确性了</b><b>
is publicly questioning the accuracy of the fund numbers.</b>

04:07.410 --> 04:08.490
<b>有什么好消息吗?</b><b>
Anything good?</b>

04:09.330 --> 04:13.000
<b>这是一只红尾鹰 今年头回看到</b><b>
It's a red-tailed hawk, first one this year.</b>

04:13.250 --> 04:14.420
<b>迪克·富尔德在1号线上等着</b><b>
Dick Fuld's on one.</b>

04:14.500 --> 04:16.750
<b>提供可信的答案</b><b>
to provide credible answers.</b>

04:16.840 --> 04:18.590
<b>让我们来一起分析一下这些 呃</b><b>
So let's go through a couple of those, uh,</b>

04:18.670 --> 04:20.710
<b>被你称为差异的东西 因为...</b><b>
what you call discrepancies, because...</b>

04:25.010 --> 04:27.510
<b>- 上午的日子不好过吧?  - 我们有高收益</b><b>
- Tough morning?  - We show top-quality earnings,</b>

04:27.600 --> 04:29.850
<b>- 粉碎了所有之前的预测  - 没错</b><b>
- we beat every prediction.  - Yeah.</b>

04:29.930 --> 04:33.730
<b>这是做空者的行为 你也知道他们的一贯伎俩 先做空 然后弯曲事实</b><b>
It's the damn short-sellers. You know the game, short and distort.</b>

04:33.810 --> 04:35.850
<b>他们善于散布谣言 然后从中大赚一笔</b><b>
They're rumormongers and they're making a killing.</b>

04:36.020 --> 04:37.940
<b>你对于筹集资金有什么计划?</b><b>
What are your plans for a capital raise?</b>

04:38.150 --> 04:40.520
<b>我们想的比你更远 让我把话再讲得明白些</b><b>
We're way ahead of you. Now, let me be clear,</b>

04:42.240 --> 04:44.530
<b>我们不需要现金</b><b>
we don't need the cash.</b>

04:45.820 --> 04:48.030
<b>这是一种直觉</b><b>
You know, it's about perception.</b>

04:48.120 --> 04:49.740
<b>快说巴菲特</b><b>
Buffett, Buffett.</b>

04:51.370 --> 04:53.700
<b>我们正在考虑同沃伦·巴菲特进行接洽</b><b>
We're thinking of reaching out to Warren Buffett.</b>

04:53.790 --> 04:54.790
<b>很好</b><b>
Great.</b>

04:55.580 --> 04:58.210
<b>你和巴菲特有过交情 对吧?</b><b>
You and Buffett go back, right?</b>

04:59.380 --> 05:01.670
<b>帮帮我 给他打个电话</b><b>
Do me a favor and call him.</b>

05:01.760 --> 05:03.340
<b>告诉他雷曼兄弟有着很坚实的基础</b><b>
Tell him Lehman is rock solid.</b>

05:03.720 --> 05:07.130
<b>作为财政部长 我不能鼓动他去进行某一项的投资</b><b>
As Treasury Secretary, I can't advocate for a specific investment.</b>

05:09.720 --> 05:12.720
<b>艾琳·卡伦</b>

05:09.720 --> 05:12.720
<b>雷曼兄弟首席财务官</b>

05:10.720 --> 05:14.890
<b>汉克 你想不想让我筹集到资金?</b><b>
Hank, you want me to raise capital or not?</b>

05:15.720 --> 05:19.900
<b>2008年5月24日,星期六</b>

05:15.810 --> 05:18.480
<b>雷曼兄弟的规模要比贝尔斯登大得多</b><b>
Lehman Brothers is a hell of a lot bigger than Bear Stearns.</b>

05:18.560 --> 05:19.900
<b>市场开始恐慌了</b><b>
The market is terrified.</b>

05:20.440 --> 05:23.230
<b>我在高盛集团主政期间 从来没有想过要去</b><b>
When I was running Goldman, I never even conceived</b>

05:23.320 --> 05:25.780
<b>请求财长为我促成一笔交易</b><b>
of asking the Treasury Secretary to cut a deal for me.</b>

05:25.860 --> 05:27.280
<b>没错 但是对贝尔斯登的紧急援助造成了...</b><b>
Yeah, but the Bear bailout created...</b>

05:27.360 --> 05:28.610
<b>不要把它说成是紧急援助</b><b>
Please don't call it a bailout.</b>

05:28.700 --> 05:33.040
<b>好吧 对贝尔斯登的一揽子大规模收购援助政策</b><b>
Okay, the very large Bear Stearns purchase assistance package</b>

05:33.120 --> 05:34.830
<b>使公众产生了一种预期</b><b>
created an expectation.</b>

05:34.910 --> 05:36.580
<b>富尔德正期待您的直接介入</b><b>
Fuld's counting on direct intervention from you.</b>

05:37.040 --> 05:39.080
<b>巴菲特可以轻而易举地解决这个问题</b><b>
Buffett's a simple solution.</b>

05:39.080 --> 05:42.300
<b>吉姆·威尔金森</b>

05:39.080 --> 05:42.300
<b>财政部参谋长</b>

05:40.750 --> 05:42.090
<b>我觉得您应该去给他打这个电话</b><b>
I think you make the call.</b>

05:42.250 --> 05:44.210
<b>以什么身份呢? 他的朋友?</b><b>
As what? Warren's friend?</b>

05:44.210 --> 05:47.170
<b>以前为他提供服务的人? 还是以财长的身份?</b><b>
His former banker? The Treasury Secretary?</b>

05:47.260 --> 05:49.430
<b>不 还是让富尔德自己去打给他吧</b><b>
No. Fuld's calling him.</b>

05:49.760 --> 05:51.300
<b>希望他能介入进来 这样大家都能安心了</b><b>
Hopefully he'll jump in and we can all relax.</b>

05:51.390 --> 05:53.680
<b>安心? 我们刚刚处理了一家投资银行</b><b>
Relax? We just buried one investment bank,</b>

05:53.690 --> 05:55.350
<b>这会儿又有另一家在苟延残喘</b><b>
we got another one that's barely breathing.</b>

05:55.430 --> 05:58.190
<b>这是一场关乎信心的博弈 如果人们对雷曼兄弟失去了信心</b><b>
This is a confidence game. People lose faith in Lehman,</b>

05:58.270 --> 06:00.020
<b>那后面的银行就会像多米诺骨牌一样成片地倒下</b><b>
these banks are gonna drop like dominoes,</b>

06:00.110 --> 06:03.480
<b>而我也无法为此再做出什么了</b><b>
and I don't have the authority to do a thing about it.</b>

06:03.570 --> 06:07.110
<b>已经晚了 一切都已经太晚了</b><b>
We're late. We've been late on everything.</b>

06:07.280 --> 06:13.000
<b>尼尔·卡西卡瑞</b>

06:07.280 --> 06:13.000
<b>部长助理,处理国际事务</b>

06:07.280 --> 06:10.360
<b>尼尔的团队正在研究这样灾难即将带来的后果</b><b>
Neel's team is working on some kind of a disaster scenario.</b>

06:10.450 --> 06:12.280
<b>我们把它称为"破杯"计划</b><b>
We're calling it the "Break the Glass" plan,</b>

06:12.370 --> 06:14.490
<b>当您走投无路的时候就可以要求国会执行这项计划</b><b>
what to ask Congress for if your back's against the wall.</b>

06:14.790 --> 06:15.950
<b>钱呗</b><b>
Money.</b>

06:17.790 --> 06:19.830
<b>就是向他们要钱呗</b><b>
Is what you ask them for.</b>

06:19.830 --> 06:26.630
<b>米歇尔·戴维斯</b>

06:19.830 --> 06:26.630
<b>部长助理,处理公共事务</b>

06:21.290 --> 06:25.130
<b>问题在于 除非我们已经撞上了冰山 否则国会不会采取举措</b><b>
The problem is, Congress won't move until we've already hit the iceberg,</b>

06:25.210 --> 06:26.630
<b>而到那时 一切都已经太晚了</b><b>
and at that point, it may be too late.</b>

06:26.720 --> 06:31.590
<b>你的意思是说 我掌管着美国财政部</b><b>
So you're saying, with the full weight of the United States Treasury behind me,</b>

06:31.680 --> 06:34.930
<b>而我能做的就是去找巴菲特求助?</b><b>
all I can do is call Warren Buffett?</b>

06:35.640 --> 06:38.770
<b>嗨 巴菲特 我是汉克</b><b>
Hi, Warren. It's Hank.</b>

06:39.390 --> 06:41.560
<b>我知道你和迪克·富尔德已经谈过了</b><b>
I understand you've been talking to Dick Fuld.</b>

06:41.650 --> 06:48.000
<b>华伦·巴菲特</b>

06:41.650 --> 06:48.000
<b>世上最富有的人</b>

06:41.650 --> 06:47.400
<b>汉克 你也知道我对那些投资银行的担忧</b><b>
You know my misgivings, Hank, about investment banks.</b>

06:47.490 --> 06:50.360
<b>他们一旦开始为自己进行交易时</b><b>
As soon as they started trading for themselves,</b>

06:50.450 --> 06:52.070
<b>那些风险经理就都失控了</b><b>
the risk managers lost control.</b>

06:52.160 --> 06:54.660
<b>我和所罗门兄弟公司有过一次不太愉快的合作经历</b><b>
I had a very unpleasant time with Salomon Brothers.</b>

06:54.740 --> 06:56.830
<b>你说得有道理</b><b>
That's fair enough.</b>

06:58.330 --> 07:02.210
<b>但我们都知道投资银行向来都是一个有利可图的行业</b><b>
But we both know that investment banking is a profitable business.</b>

07:02.420 --> 07:05.840
<b>我猜它大概已经为你赚了数十亿美金了吧?</b><b>
I figure it made you a billion or so, huh?</b>

07:05.920 --> 07:10.010
<b>我相信如果他们出价合理的话 你也不会袖手旁观吧</b><b>
I gotta believe that if the price was right, you wouldn't just walk away.</b>

07:10.090 --> 07:14.680
<b>在事实面前才算数 你觉得呢?</b><b>
You know a good deal when you see one. What say you?</b>

07:14.930 --> 07:17.560
<b>还是你自己来判断吧</b><b>
I gotta leave that to your judgment.</b>

07:18.680 --> 07:20.980
<b>大家的反应就好像我们是奸商一样</b><b>
People act like we're crack dealers.</b>

07:21.060 --> 07:22.810
<b>没人拿着枪去指向某人说</b><b>
Nobody put a gun to anybody's head and said,</b>

07:22.900 --> 07:26.320
<b>"嘿 猎人 买下这栋你偿还不起的房子吧 等你住进去以后</b><b>
"Hey, nimrod, buy a house you can't afford. And you know what? While you're at it,</b>

07:26.400 --> 07:28.440
<b>再用它申请信用额度 这件就可以再买一艘船了"</b><b>
put a line of credit on that baby and buy yourself a boat."</b>

07:28.690 --> 07:30.950
<b>巴菲特给你回复了吗?</b><b>
You heard anything from Buffett?</b>

07:31.240 --> 07:35.490
<b>他要求获得股价为40美金的优先股 分红为9%</b><b>
He's asking for preferred shares at 40 with a dividend of 9%.</b>

07:35.580 --> 07:37.990
<b>股价刚还在66块呢 搞什么鬼啊?</b><b>
We were just at 66. What the fuck?</b>

07:38.080 --> 07:40.040
<b>或许这只是游戏的序幕吧 迪克</b><b>
Maybe it's just an opening gambit, Dick.</b>

07:40.160 --> 07:41.710
<b>听上去更像是一种侮辱</b><b>
Sounds more like a goddamn insult.</b>

07:41.790 --> 07:43.210
<b>- 我来帮你弄吧 迪克  - 谢谢</b><b>
- Let me get that, Dick.  - Thank you.</b>

07:43.380 --> 07:45.330
<b>我们的股价已经跌到了36块</b><b>
We're at 36 right now.</b>

07:45.880 --> 07:48.750
<b>这几个月以来我们从未到过66快附近</b><b>
We haven't been anywhere near 66 in months.</b>

07:48.840 --> 07:50.760
<b>市场喜欢巴菲特</b><b>
The markets like Buffett.</b>

07:50.840 --> 07:53.630
<b>- 他的名字会在一夜之间推动股价上升  - 我才不在乎他是谁</b><b>
- His name will push the price up overnight.  - I don't care who he is,</b>

07:53.800 --> 07:58.810
<b>我不会用1年花费3亿6000万的代价去取悦他以谋求合作</b><b>
I am not spending $360 million a year for the pleasure of doing business with him.</b>

07:58.890 --> 08:00.020
<b>房地产市场会重新振作起来的</b><b>
Real estate will come back.</b>

08:00.100 --> 08:01.640
<b>韩国人有意介入</b><b>
Koreans have been sniffing around.</b>

08:01.730 --> 08:03.520
<b>这不好了 他们不会漫天要价</b><b>
There you go. And they won't steal us blind.</b>

08:03.600 --> 08:06.360
<b>这种场面以前我也经历过 首席执行官们开始恐慌 然后廉价卖掉自己的股票</b><b>
I've seen this before. CEOs panic and they sell out cheap.</b>

08:06.440 --> 08:09.440
<b>现在 整条华尔街都认为已经到了火烧眉毛的时候</b><b>
Right now, the Street's running around with its hair on fire,</b>

08:09.530 --> 08:11.400
<b>但暴风雨总会过去的</b><b>
but the storm always passes.</b>

08:11.490 --> 08:16.120
<b>我们要充满信心 然后 去参加高盛举办的午宴</b><b>
We stand strong, and on the other side, we'll eat Goldman's lunch.</b>

08:18.160 --> 08:19.910
<b>那我们该如何回复巴菲特呢?</b><b>
So, what do we do about Buffett?</b>

08:20.660 --> 08:23.620
<b>去他妈的巴菲特</b><b>
Screw Warren Buffett.</b>

08:25.790 --> 08:26.820
<b>每周早餐会议</b>

08:25.790 --> 08:27.420
<b>- 他拒绝了?  - 雷曼兄弟的股价</b><b>
- He passed?  - Lehman dropped.</b>

08:27.500 --> 08:29.750
<b>在今天上午已经跌到了28块半 他到底是怎么想的啊?</b><b>
to 28 and a half this morning. What in the world is he thinking?</b>

08:29.840 --> 08:33.840
<b>他根本没有思考 他是在妄想 他认为巴菲特的开价太高了</b><b>
He's not thinking. He's delusional. He thought the ask was too high.</b>

08:34.240 --> 08:38.600
<b>本·伯南克</b>

08:34.240 --> 08:38.600
<b>联邦储蓄主席</b>

08:35.260 --> 08:36.680
<b>他得去筹措资金啊</b><b>
He's gotta raise cash.</b>

08:36.760 --> 08:38.600
<b>我也是这么跟他说的</b><b>
I told him that.</b>

08:39.930 --> 08:42.100
<b>- 我找格林斯潘谈过了  - 真的吗?</b><b>
- I spoke to Greenspan.  - Really?</b>

08:42.310 --> 08:47.560
<b>他说住房市场供过于求 这就是问题所在</b><b>
He says there's too much housing supply. That's the problem.</b>

08:48.860 --> 08:53.440
<b>所以我们应该买下所有闲置房屋 不让它们流入市场</b><b>
So we should buy up all the vacant houses and burn them.</b>

09:00.660 --> 09:03.950
<b>迪克需要一个能认清现状的买家</b><b>
Dick needs a buyer, someone with a grip on reality.</b>

09:04.120 --> 09:06.290
<b>几个月前巴克莱银行曾表示过些许兴趣</b><b>
Barclays expressed some interest a couple of months ago,</b>

09:06.370 --> 09:08.130
<b>但我觉得现在的股价还没有降到他们的心理价位</b><b>
but I don't think the price is low enough for them.</b>

09:09.000 --> 09:11.210
<b>- 美国银行呢?  - 有这个可能</b><b>
- Bank of America?  - Possible.</b>

09:11.300 --> 09:13.170
<b>迪克之前也试探过他们</b><b>
Dick's put out feelers there before.</b>

09:13.720 --> 09:15.840
<b>不过我们得保持低调</b><b>
We have to keep it quiet, though.</b>

09:15.930 --> 09:17.930
<b>因为一旦有人获悉他们准备出售</b><b>
'Cause if anyone hears that they're trying to sell</b>

09:18.140 --> 09:20.970
<b>雷曼兄弟将瞬间完蛋</b><b>
Lehman'll be dead within the hour.</b>

09:21.310 --> 09:26.390
<b>2008年6月11日,雷曼兄弟高管紧急决策会议</b>

09:21.310 --> 09:23.470
<b>在房地产业务上的投资正在毁掉整个公司</b><b>
The real estate investments are killing the firm.</b>

09:24.140 --> 09:26.390
<b>我们得公开承认我们犯了一些错误</b><b>
We have to admit publically we've made some mistakes.</b>

09:26.560 --> 09:28.520
<b>我们需要对高管层进行更替</b><b>
We need to make a senior management change,</b>

09:28.610 --> 09:30.690
<b>从而向市场表明我们的立场</b><b>
signal to the market that we get it.</b>

09:32.230 --> 09:35.400
<b>- 你们指的是谁?  - 乔·格雷戈里</b><b>
- Meaning what?  - Meaning Joe Gregory.</b>

09:35.990 --> 09:38.450
<b>别扯淡了</b><b>
Get the fuck out of here.</b>

09:40.030 --> 09:41.830
<b>还轮不到你们来告诉我该如何来运营我的公司</b><b>
You are not gonna tell me how to run my company.</b>

09:41.950 --> 09:44.910
<b>乔在这场危机中没有站在你这边 这是人所共知的</b><b>
Joe hasn't had your back on risk, and everyone knows it.</b>

09:45.000 --> 09:48.330
<b>艾琳·卡伦也得走人 整条华尔街都知道她就是个笑话</b><b>
Erin Callan's gotta go, too. As far as the Street's concerned, she's a joke.</b>

09:48.460 --> 09:52.340
<b>乔·格雷戈里和我共事了30多年</b><b>
Joe Gregory has been with me for 30 years.</b>

09:53.510 --> 09:57.010
<b>我们只是遇到了暂时性的困难 你们就想让我把他撵走?</b><b>
And you want me to kick him to the curb because we had a bad quarter?</b>

09:57.090 --> 09:58.630
<b>这不是暂时性的困难</b><b>
It's not just a bad quarter.</b>

09:58.720 --> 10:00.680
<b>股价已经跌到23块了</b><b>
Stock hit 23.</b>

10:00.760 --> 10:07.310
<b>斯基普·麦基</b>

10:00.760 --> 10:07.310
<b>雷曼兄弟投行部,全球区总裁</b>

10:00.760 --> 10:04.310
<b>23块啊 公司大部分员工分到的股票都是在数年内无法进行买卖的</b><b>
Twenty-three. Most of our guys are paid in stock they can't sell for years.</b>

10:04.390 --> 10:07.020
<b>他们损失的是过去六个月里赚的净利润</b><b>
They've lost most of their net worth over the last six months.</b>

10:07.520 --> 10:11.060
<b>如果你不稳住股价 你的那些交易员们只能跑路了</b><b>
You don't stabilize the price, your traders are gonna jump ship.</b>

10:11.230 --> 10:13.020
<b>一群自私鬼</b><b>
Selfish fucks.</b>

10:13.110 --> 10:16.990
<b>迪克 不仅是银行家和交易员们 连客户都会抽走他们的资金</b><b>
It's not just bankers and traders, Dick. Clients are pulling their money.</b>

10:17.200 --> 10:19.780
<b>公司将遭遇到连锁反应</b><b>
There's gonna be a run on this bank.</b>

10:23.540 --> 10:25.540
<b>消息灵通人士对财经频道透露</b><b>
Sources tell CNBC that both</b>

10:25.620 --> 10:29.250
<b>雷曼兄弟的艾琳·卡伦和乔瑟夫·格雷戈里已经离任</b><b>
Erin Callan and Joseph Gregory are out at Lehman Brothers.</b>

10:29.370 --> 10:31.750
<b>公司的主席迪克·富尔德在一份声明中称</b><b>
In a statement, the company's chairman, Dick Fuld, said</b>

10:31.840 --> 10:33.550
<b>2008年8月4日</b>

10:31.840 --> 10:34.750
<b>将由48岁的巴特·迈克达德代替格雷戈里的位子</b><b>
replacing Gregory with 48-year-old Bart McDade</b>

10:34.750 --> 10:40.090
<b>巴特·迈克达德</b>

10:34.750 --> 10:40.090
<b>雷曼兄弟新总裁兼首席运营官</b>

10:34.840 --> 10:38.090
<b>这是他所做过的最艰难的一个决定</b><b>
has been one of the most difficult decisions he's had to make.</b>

10:39.800 --> 10:42.550
<b>迪克 韩国人刚刚到达苏里文</b><b>
Dick, the Koreans just arrived at Sullivan.</b>

10:43.680 --> 10:44.850
<b>我们一定要抓住这次机会</b><b>
Let's go make this happen.</b>

10:45.390 --> 10:47.730
<b>我觉得这会儿你最好就待在这里</b><b>
My take is you'd be better off staying here for now.</b>

10:49.560 --> 10:51.350
<b>我们要把你打造成为"幕后人士"</b><b>
We need you to be our "missing man."</b>

10:51.900 --> 10:54.320
<b>由我们去谈 尽最大努力去促成这笔交易</b><b>
We'll go in and push the deal as far as we can,</b>

10:54.400 --> 10:57.990
<b>最后再由你出面来达成这笔交易</b><b>
and then we'll bring you in at the end to top it off.</b>

10:58.150 --> 10:59.400
<b>好吧 听你的</b><b>
All right, fine.</b>

11:00.530 --> 11:02.320
<b>很好</b><b>
Okay. Okay.</b>

11:07.910 --> 11:10.540
<b>我们如期来到了纽约</b><b>
We are committed to our presence in New York.</b>

11:12.880 --> 11:15.920
<b>但我们需要知道确切的数字</b><b>
But we need to know that the underlying numbers make sense.</b>

11:19.260 --> 11:21.930
<b>我们也看到了事情的发展情况</b><b>
We realize how things look.</b>

11:22.010 --> 11:24.220
<b>但我们的股价只是被一些做空者暂时挫伤</b><b>
But our stock is getting hammered by the shorts.</b>

11:24.640 --> 11:26.100
<b>它的真实价值依旧没变</b><b>
The value is still there.</b>

11:28.100 --> 11:31.560
<b>我们刚刚开始谈 闵还是很兴奋的 但他们还没有给出具体的数字</b><b>
We just started. Min's excited, but we haven't heard the terms.</b>

11:33.150 --> 11:34.230
<b>你在哪儿?</b><b>
Where are you?</b>

11:34.310 --> 11:35.940
<b>我刚走出会议室来接你的电话啊</b><b>
I just stepped out to take the call.</b>

11:36.820 --> 11:38.480
<b>快回去 要有礼貌啊</b><b>
Get back in there. Don't be rude.</b>

11:39.780 --> 11:41.570
<b>好的</b><b>
Okay.</b>

11:41.650 --> 11:44.490
<b>我们只是将你们不感兴趣的那一部分资产</b><b>
We simply take the assets you don't find appealing,</b>

11:45.530 --> 11:47.660
<b>拆分成一个独立的公司</b><b>
spin them off into a separate company.</b>

11:49.950 --> 11:52.410
<b>- 你不必买下整家银行  - 抱歉</b><b>
- You don't buy that bank.  - I'm very sorry.</b>

11:52.500 --> 11:54.420
<b>你只需买下这家运营良好的银行就行了</b><b>
You buy the good bank.</b>

11:57.210 --> 11:58.710
<b>他们对房地产不感兴趣</b><b>
Look, they don't like the real estate.</b>

11:58.800 --> 12:00.130
<b>什么叫他们不感兴趣?</b><b>
What do you mean, they don't like it?</b>

12:00.220 --> 12:03.970
<b>迪克 我们终于有些进展了 暂时不要打扰我了</b><b>
Dick, we're making real progress here, okay? Let me stay on it for now.</b>

12:20.030 --> 12:22.150
<b>闵 你好</b><b>
Min, how are you?</b>

12:22.700 --> 12:24.570
<b>很高兴见到你</b><b>
Great to see you.</b>

12:25.530 --> 12:27.120
<b>希望没有打扰到你们</b><b>
I don't want to interrupt.</b>

12:27.410 --> 12:29.540
<b>迪克 你来得正是时候</b><b>
Dick, great timing.</b>

12:29.620 --> 12:32.160
<b>看起来双方对合同的大致框架都很满意</b><b>
We seem to be in sync on the broad strokes of the deal.</b>

12:32.710 --> 12:34.710
<b>我们可以回到意向书上来了吗?</b><b>
Shall we get back to the letter of intent?</b>

12:34.870 --> 12:39.670
<b>闵 我不得不告诉你 我觉得你正在犯一个大错</b><b>
Min, I have to tell you, I think you're making a big mistake here.</b>

12:39.840 --> 12:42.340
<b>房地产资产价值巨大</b><b>
There's great value in the real estate assets.</b>

12:43.550 --> 12:45.510
<b>要不通过仔细分析投资组合</b><b>
How about we walk through the portfolio</b>

12:46.180 --> 12:47.680
<b>我来向你展示这一点如何?</b><b>
and I'll show you?</b>

12:50.560 --> 12:52.350
<b>我们已经仔细看过了</b><b>
We have looked at them.</b>

12:52.430 --> 12:56.020
<b>有些地方你肯定没看懂</b><b>
Then you must have looked at them in the wrong way.</b>

12:56.860 --> 12:59.650
<b>我不想看你做出错误的决定</b><b>
See, I just don't wanna see you leave money on the table.</b>

12:59.730 --> 13:02.360
<b>或许我们应该休息一下</b><b>
Perhaps we should take a break.</b>

13:08.320 --> 13:10.450
<b>闵 非常抱歉</b><b>
Min, I'm so sorry.</b>

13:10.540 --> 13:14.660
<b>我们一直在真心实意地进行谈判 突然就这么回到原点了?</b><b>
We have negotiated in good faith. Now all of a sudden we are going backward?</b>

13:14.750 --> 13:16.290
<b>我们同意你给出的报价</b><b>
We can work with you on the price.</b>

13:16.370 --> 13:18.210
<b>这与报价无关</b><b>
It is not about the price.</b>

13:18.590 --> 13:22.000
<b>我说的是你们处理事情的方式</b><b>
It is about the way you have conducted this.</b>

13:27.680 --> 13:30.640
<b>非常感谢大家</b><b>
I'd like to thank you, all of you,</b>

13:30.930 --> 13:34.220
<b>但我觉得已经没有继续谈下去的基础了</b><b>
but I don't think we have a structure that works.</b>

13:40.440 --> 13:41.650
<b>什么 就这么结束了?</b><b>
What, that's it?</b>

13:41.730 --> 13:43.530
<b>你们就打算这么打道回府了?</b><b>
You're just gonna pack up and go back to Korea?</b>

13:57.500 --> 13:59.460
<b>- 你好  - 尼尔 我是迪克·富尔德</b><b>
- Hello?  - Neel, it's Dick Fuld.</b>

14:01.090 --> 14:04.710
<b>听着 如果汉克想让我找到买家</b><b>
Listen, you know, if Hank wants me to find a buyer,</b>

14:04.800 --> 14:06.260
<b>你们得出面帮我一把啊</b><b>
you guys need to step up and help.</b>

14:06.630 --> 14:08.930
<b>韩国人刚刚退出交易了</b><b>
The Koreans just walked out, okay?</b>

14:09.090 --> 14:10.640
<b>我只是表达一下自己的观点</b><b>
Look, I'm just speaking for myself here,</b>

14:10.720 --> 14:13.060
<b>但我认为你应该做一些有利于公司的事情</b><b>
but I think you need to do what's right for the firm.</b>

14:13.140 --> 14:14.850
<b>什么叫有利于?</b><b>
Do what's right?</b>

14:14.930 --> 14:16.430
<b>这话是什么意思?</b><b>
What is that supposed to mean?</b>

14:16.600 --> 14:18.690
<b>如果股价继续下跌</b><b>
If your stock price keeps sliding,</b>

14:18.770 --> 14:21.230
<b>你也许会得到一个令人失望的报价</b><b>
you may get an offer at a price that doesn't look all that compelling,</b>

14:21.310 --> 14:24.270
<b>但为了公司的持续经营 你必须接受它</b><b>
but you may have to take it just to keep the company intact.</b>

14:24.690 --> 14:26.030
<b>你指什么样的买价?</b><b>
What kind of price are you talking about?</b>

14:26.280 --> 14:27.690
<b>可能会...</b><b>
Could be...</b>

14:27.780 --> 14:30.070
<b>我指 股价可能在个位数</b><b>
I mean, it might be low single digits.</b>

14:32.660 --> 14:36.330
<b>二月份 我们公司每股66美元</b><b>
Last February, we were at 66 a share.</b>

14:38.330 --> 14:42.580
<b>雷曼兄弟可不是贝尔斯登</b><b>
Lehman Brothers is not Bear Stearns.</b>

14:42.670 --> 14:46.130
<b>我们业绩很好的 房地产会复苏的</b><b>
We've got a great business. Real estate's gonna come back.</b>

14:46.260 --> 14:49.260
<b>我他妈不会把这公司送人的!</b><b>
I am not fucking giving this company away!</b>

14:49.760 --> 14:51.000
<b>在雷曼兄弟股价因其</b><b>
While the real estate market has put</b>

14:51.000 --> 14:52.550
<b>房地产业务而备受压力时</b><b>
put Lehman Brothers shares under pressure,</b>

14:52.640 --> 14:54.720
<b>房贷巨头房利美和房地美两公司传出报道说</b><b>
mortgage giants Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac stocks</b>

14:54.810 --> 14:58.100
<b>需要筹资750亿美元才能偿付其债务 </b><b>
are suddenly plummeting this morning, after reports the companies</b>

14:58.180 --> 15:02.060
<b>此后 这两家公司的股价急剧下跌</b><b>
may need to raise $75 billion just to remain solvent.</b>

15:02.150 --> 15:04.400
<b>因为这两家公司几乎担保了</b><b>
Because they guarantee such an enormous percentage</b>

15:04.480 --> 15:05.900
<b>全国大部分的次级贷款</b><b>
of the nation's mortgages,</b>

15:05.980 --> 15:07.730
<b>有关人士预测政府将会介入</b><b>
there is renewed speculation that the government</b>

15:07.820 --> 15:09.820
<b>该事态中 收购两家公司</b><b>
may have to step in and take them over,</b>

15:10.240 --> 15:13.620
<b>政府介入的可能性也从奥巴马的竞选演讲中得到证实</b><b>
a possibility Barack Obama has now raised on the campaign trail.</b>

15:13.700 --> 15:16.410
<b>若房利美和房地美倒闭了</b><b>
If Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac collapsed,</b>

15:16.490 --> 15:22.580
<b>那么将会给整个金融界带来</b><b>
then probably the financial system would receive such a body blow</b>

15:22.670 --> 15:25.170
<b>灾难性的动荡</b><b>
that it could be disastrous.</b>

15:25.500 --> 15:29.510
<b>房地美下跌了8% 房利美下跌5%</b><b>
Freddie just dropped another 8%. Fannie's down 5%.</b>

15:29.500 --> 15:35.010
<b>蒂莫西·盖特纳</b>

15:29.500 --> 15:35.010
<b>纽约联邦储备银行行长</b>

15:30.130 --> 15:34.800
<b>下跌趋势迅猛 我们得采取措施了 立刻</b><b>
There's no bottom here. We need to do something. Now.</b>

15:36.260 --> 15:37.930
<b>我们正向国会提议</b><b>
We're working on a proposal for Congress,</b>

15:38.020 --> 15:40.730
<b>看能否批准我们向市场注资救市</b><b>
see if we can get the authority to put some money in.</b>

15:40.810 --> 15:44.980
<b>我本不想这么做的 但若情况特别糟糕的话...</b><b>
I'd rather not go that way, but if we get there...</b>

15:45.060 --> 15:47.770
<b>我想事态已经很糟糕了</b><b>
I think we're already there.</b>

15:49.740 --> 15:52.610
<b>- 你能要到多少?  - 一张空白支票</b><b>
- How much are you gonna ask for?  - A blank check.</b>

15:53.320 --> 15:56.700
<b>投资资金必须足以让我们挽救市场</b><b>
It has to be enough of a statement to reassure the market.</b>

15:56.780 --> 16:00.500
<b>得让市场觉得 我拥有决定性武器</b><b>
They need to think I've got a bazooka in my pocket.</b>

16:00.580 --> 16:04.670
<b>不是说我们真的会注资 只是如果我们得到了国会的许可</b><b>
I'm not saying that we use it, but if we have the authority,</b>

16:04.750 --> 16:08.500
<b>那么 所有疯狂抛售股票的人会逐渐冷静下来 重新参与</b><b>
everyone who's dumping their shares will calm down, back off.</b>

16:09.380 --> 16:12.050
<b>行 若你在国会 你也可以顺便提议资助那些投资银行 是吧?</b><b>
Okay, if you're going to Congress, why don't we give to the banks, too?</b>

16:12.130 --> 16:14.380
<b>因为雷曼兄弟眼看活不成了 美林也离破产不远了</b><b>
'Cause Lehman's looking like shit and Merrill's not far behind.</b>

16:14.550 --> 16:17.220
<b>光说服他们愿意接管房利美和房地美就够走运了</b><b>
We'll be lucky to get them to move on Fannie and Freddie.</b>

16:17.310 --> 16:19.680
<b>我们只能说试试看</b><b>
We do what we can do.</b>

16:22.310 --> 16:28.080
<b>2008年8月8日,北京奥运会开幕式</b>

16:30.900 --> 16:33.360
<b>部长先生 部长夫人 请看这边</b><b>
Secretary, Mrs. Paulson, over here.</b>

16:33.910 --> 16:35.280
<b>请看这边 谢谢</b><b>
Over here, please.</b>

16:38.740 --> 16:39.950
<b>保尔森部长 请看这边 谢谢</b><b>
Secretary Paulson, over here, please.</b>

16:40.040 --> 16:41.830
<b>保尔森夫人 谢谢</b><b>
Mrs. Paulson. Thank you.</b>

16:45.080 --> 16:46.540
<b>保尔森夫人</b><b>
Mr. Paulson.</b>

16:46.630 --> 16:49.130
<b>保尔森部长 夫人 请看这边 谢谢</b><b>
Mr. and Mrs. Paulson, this way, please.</b>

16:54.590 --> 16:56.300
<b>- 我来抱着  - 带她先去一边</b><b>
- I've got her.  - You should take her.</b>

16:57.930 --> 16:59.760
<b>请看这边 保尔森部长 谢谢</b><b>
Right over here, Secretary Paulson, please.</b>

17:01.020 --> 17:02.100
<b>请笑一笑 谢谢</b><b>
Big smile. Thank you.</b>

17:02.850 --> 17:04.180
<b>这正是我需要的</b><b>
That's just what I need.</b>

17:04.270 --> 17:07.310
<b>新闻媒体拍到美国财政部长居然挥舞着中国国旗</b><b>
Press photos of the Treasury Secretary waving the Chinese flag.</b>

17:07.400 --> 17:12.440
<b>保尔森竟然是共产党员 你当时脸上的表情很精彩的</b><b>
Paulson the Communist. The look on your face was priceless.</b>

17:14.400 --> 17:17.160
<b>汉克 关于房利美和房地美 我有问题要问</b><b>
Hank, I must ask you about Fannie and Freddie.</b>

17:19.910 --> 17:22.160
<b>我们在"两房"公司投资了数十亿美元</b><b>
We have hundreds of billions invested.</b>

17:22.160 --> 17:25.160
<b>你和我保证过投资是安全的</b><b>
You've assured us the investment is safe.</b>

17:25.250 --> 17:28.040
<b>是的 绝对安全</b><b>
And it is, absolutely.</b>

17:29.420 --> 17:32.550
<b>可我们发现 近期损失了很大一笔数额</b><b>
We're watching a great deal of our money disappear.</b>

17:32.630 --> 17:36.720
<b>两个月内 股价竟然跌了60%</b><b>
Share prices have dropped 60% in the last two months.</b>

17:36.800 --> 17:39.300
<b>光到处宣扬你有决定性武器可以救市是不够的</b><b>
Carrying your bazooka around has not helped matters.</b>

17:40.350 --> 17:43.560
<b>国会给了你权利 也许是时候使用这项权利了</b><b>
Congress gave you the power. Perhaps it is time to use it.</b>

17:43.640 --> 17:47.390
<b>市场会稳定下来的 需要的只是时间而已</b><b>
The market will stabilize. We just have to give it some time.</b>

17:47.850 --> 17:51.360
<b>俄罗斯上个月和我们联系</b><b>
There was an approach last month from Russia.</b>

17:52.480 --> 17:55.240
<b>他们也持有大量房利美和房地美的的债券</b><b>
They have considerable holdings in Fannie and Freddie as well.</b>

17:56.240 --> 17:58.910
<b>俄罗斯建议我和他们合作 搞一次突击 </b><b>
They suggested we coordinate, and without warning,</b>

17:58.990 --> 18:00.610
<b>向市场大量抛售房利美</b><b>
dump hundreds of billions of Fannie</b>

18:00.610 --> 18:02.410
<b>和房地美的债卷</b><b>
and Freddie's bonds onto the market.</b>

18:05.910 --> 18:07.870
<b>- 那市场就会...  - 一片混乱</b><b>
- That would be...  - Chaos.</b>

18:08.830 --> 18:12.000
<b>贵国发售过多的债卷</b><b>
The amount of debt your country carries</b>

18:12.000 --> 18:13.380
<b>是你们一处致命的弱点</b><b>
is a terrible vulnerability.</b>

18:19.140 --> 18:22.760
<b>- 但你们...  - 我们很客气地拒绝了</b><b>
- But you...  - We declined, respectfully.</b>

18:25.520 --> 18:27.600
<b>即使是在美国</b><b>
Even in the US, it seems</b>

18:27.690 --> 18:29.560
<b>你们政府和非国营企业</b><b>
the relationship between the government</b>

18:29.560 --> 18:32.360
<b>的关系似乎也是挺复杂的</b><b>
and private industry isn't so simple.</b>

18:36.610 --> 18:38.240
<b>他在威胁我们?</b><b>
Was it a threat?</b>

18:38.320 --> 18:41.950
<b>不 不是 只能算一个友情提示</b><b>
No, no, it was a friendly reminder</b>

18:42.030 --> 18:44.000
<b>提示我们 只要他们给莫斯科打一个电话</b><b>
that with a single phone call to Moscow,</b>

18:44.000 --> 18:45.990
<b>我们美国经济就会全面崩溃</b><b>
they can take down the entire US economy.</b>

18:53.880 --> 18:58.470
<b>从账面来看 房利美和房地美简直就是一团糟</b><b>
The book says Fannie and Freddie are a nightmare.</b>

18:58.550 --> 19:01.220
<b>负债缺口至少有数百亿美元</b><b>
They are in the hole easily tens of billions of dollars.</b>

19:01.300 --> 19:03.550
<b>过不了几周 他们就无法偿还债务了</b><b>
Another few weeks, they're gonna start defaulting on their debts.</b>

19:03.640 --> 19:04.860
<b>政府得介入干预此事了</b><b>
We're gonna have to step in.</b>

19:04.860 --> 19:07.560
<b>我不明白该怎么做</b><b>
I don't see how we can avoid it.</b>

19:10.350 --> 19:13.560
<b>看来武器不开一枪是震慑不住市场的</b><b>
Turns out a bazooka's not that useful unless you fire it.</b>

19:15.650 --> 19:17.690
<b>雷曼兄弟股价又跌了10%</b><b>
Lehman's down another 10%.</b>

19:17.780 --> 19:20.320
<b>你就不让我安心地咬一口面包 是吧?</b><b>
You are not gonna let me get down a single bite, are you?</b>

19:20.400 --> 19:21.610
<b>所以我早餐吃燕麦粥</b><b>
This is why I have oatmeal.</b>

19:21.700 --> 19:24.320
<b>迪克现在正满世界地乞求援助</b><b>
Dick is trotting around the world with his hat in his hands,</b>

19:24.410 --> 19:26.160
<b>但就是没人给他钱</b><b>
no one will give him any money.</b>

19:26.240 --> 19:28.330
<b>韩国老板放弃了他 墨西哥人叫他别管了</b><b>
Korea walked out on him. Mexico told him to shove it.</b>

19:28.410 --> 19:30.540
<b>没人对他公司感兴趣 所有能忽悠到的融资早就入股了</b><b>
No one's interested. All the dumb money's already in.</b>

19:30.620 --> 19:32.420
<b>那找美国银行如何? 他们还有兴趣吧?</b><b>
What about B of A? Are they still in the mix?</b>

19:32.540 --> 19:35.170
<b>巴克莱银行也开始蠢蠢欲动了</b><b>
And Barclays is sniffing around again,</b>

19:35.170 --> 19:36.670
<b>他们认为此时是买入的好时机</b><b>
now that they think it's a fire sale.</b>

19:36.750 --> 19:38.550
<b>- 这倒不错  - 鬼知道</b><b>
- That's promising.  - I don't know.</b>

19:38.630 --> 19:42.340
<b>那些英国佬光会说说 从未付诸行动</b><b>
The British, they do a lot of talking. They never close.</b>

19:44.350 --> 19:47.310
<b>- 美国银行是目前最好的收购者了  - 雷曼不能步贝尔斯登后尘</b><b>
- B of A is still our best bet.  - This can't be another Bear.</b>

19:47.390 --> 19:50.350
<b>不会的 他们会认购雷曼的全部股份</b><b>
Absolutely not. They want Lehman, they buy it outright.</b>

19:50.430 --> 19:52.100
<b>但他们需要我们经济上的帮助</b><b>
But they may need a little hand-holding, though.</b>

19:52.190 --> 19:54.650
<b>因为他们才收购了美国国家金融服务公司 所以口袋里有点紧</b><b>
They just bought Countrywide. They're spread a little thin.</b>

19:55.110 --> 19:58.280
<b>央行对美国银行资本充足率要求得暂时松一松</b><b>
You may have to give them a break with the capital requirements.</b>

19:58.440 --> 20:01.740
<b>你想让我允许美国银行提高他们的杠杆比率</b><b>
You want me to allow them to raise their leverage</b>

20:01.820 --> 20:03.280
<b>这样他们就能收购另一家</b><b>
so they can buy a bank that's about</b>

20:03.280 --> 20:05.280
<b>因杠杆比率过高而即将破产的银行?</b><b>
to fail because it was overleveraged?</b>

20:06.950 --> 20:08.950
<b>你有更好意见?</b><b>
You got a better idea?</b>

20:09.750 --> 20:12.460
<b>突发新闻刚刚传来 财经频道刚刚收到消息</b><b>
Breaking news just coming in. Sources telling CNBC</b>

20:12.460 --> 20:14.570
<b>政府最近宣布接管</b><b>
that the government has just taken</b>

20:14.570 --> 20:16.840
<b>房利美和房地美公司</b><b>
control of Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac.</b>

20:16.920 --> 20:18.880
<b>然而在七月份 您可能会记起 汉克·保尔森曾说过</b><b>
Back in July, you remember, Hank Paulson said</b>

20:18.960 --> 20:20.520
<b>他想让通过此举来介入</b><b>
that he wanted the power to step in,</b>

20:20.520 --> 20:22.720
<b>但他可能不会采取行动</b><b>
but he probably wouldn't use it.</b>

20:22.800 --> 20:24.340
<b>现在看来保尔森</b><b>
It certainly sounds like Paulson</b>

20:24.350 --> 20:26.340
<b>不得不用起他手里的武器了</b><b>
just pulled the trigger on that bazooka.</b>

20:26.430 --> 20:28.430
<b>虽然房利美和房地美公司正在进行国有化</b><b>
Despite the move to nationalize Fannie and Freddie,</b>

20:27.850 --> 20:35.020
<b>2008年9月11号,纽约市区</b>

20:28.510 --> 20:31.770
<b>但股市仍然全盘处于下跌状态</b><b>
the market is still in negative territory across the board.</b>

20:31.850 --> 20:35.020
<b>投资者们现在正关注雷曼兄弟的命运</b><b>
Investors now focusing their attention on Lehman Brothers,</b>

20:35.100 --> 20:36.880
<b>尤其是有传言说 这家美国</b><b>
amid fresh reports that the nation's</b>

20:36.880 --> 20:38.480
<b>第四大投资银行</b><b>
fourth-largest investment bank</b>

20:38.570 --> 20:40.280
<b>正处于破产边缘</b><b>
may be on the brink of bankruptcy.</b>

20:40.480 --> 20:41.900
<b>嘿 罗奇</b><b>
Rodge.</b>

20:41.990 --> 20:43.490
<b>你好 克里斯</b><b>
Chris.</b>

20:43.570 --> 20:45.030
<b>今天带钱来了 对吧?</b><b>
Bring your money today, huh?</b>

20:47.570 --> 20:50.030
<b>克里斯·弗劳尔斯</b>

20:47.570 --> 20:50.030
<b>银行收购专家</b>

20:48.620 --> 20:51.290
<b>别让富尔德再隐藏什么对公司不好的消息了</b><b>
Make sure Fuld's not keeping any bad news out of the mix.</b>

20:51.370 --> 20:54.660
<b>罗基·科恩</b>

20:51.370 --> 20:54.660
<b>雷曼兄弟辩护律师</b>

20:51.370 --> 20:54.330
<b>用迪克的话来说就是"大白于天下"</b><b>
It's "open kimono," to quote Dick.</b>

20:54.670 --> 20:55.830
<b>他让人讨厌</b><b>
There's a revolting image.</b>

20:59.500 --> 21:02.460
<b>你研究他们的数据了吗?</b><b>
Did, uh, you get a look at the numbers?</b>

21:03.050 --> 21:05.970
<b>房地产资产是个问题 他们对其定价300亿美元</b><b>
The real estate's the issue. They got it marked at 30 billion.</b>

21:06.050 --> 21:10.060
<b>估计高估了一半 别这么紧张</b><b>
It's worth maybe half of that. Don't look so nervous.</b>

21:10.140 --> 21:11.650
<b>你们只需要花买一个热狗的钱</b><b>
You're about to get a Wall Street</b>

21:11.650 --> 21:13.350
<b>就能买到这家华尔街的投资银行</b><b>
bank for the price of a hot dog.</b>

21:13.850 --> 21:15.580
<b>我知道保尔森和肯·路易斯(美国银行首席执行官)</b><b>
I know that Paulson told Ken Lewis</b>

21:14.080 --> 21:19.980
<b>葛瑞格·克尔</b>

21:14.080 --> 21:19.980
<b>美国银行策划部部长</b>

21:15.580 --> 21:16.980
<b>说过他不会介入此收购的</b><b>
that he's not gonna pay for this.</b>

21:17.060 --> 21:18.610
<b>若政府不出面接管一些不良资产的话</b><b>
And I don't see how we can do it</b>

21:18.690 --> 21:20.570
<b>我想我们还是无法收购雷曼的</b><b>
unless the government takes some of the downside.</b>

21:20.860 --> 21:22.650
<b>保尔森只是故作姿态</b><b>
Paulson is posturing.</b>

21:22.740 --> 21:24.780
<b>他会给你支票的 就像他曾让摩根大通</b><b>
He'll write a check just like he did</b>

21:24.780 --> 21:25.780
<b>收购贝尔斯登时一样</b><b>
for Jamie Dimon on the Bear deal.</b>

21:25.860 --> 21:26.580
<b>他必须这么做</b><b>
He has to.</b>

21:26.580 --> 21:29.780
<b>他可不能在总统竞选年度再损失一家大型投行了</b><b>
He can't lose another major bank in an election year.</b>

21:29.870 --> 21:31.590
<b>而且 那家伙在高盛的时候</b><b>
Besides, the guy made, like, a half</b>

21:31.590 --> 21:34.290
<b>最起码赚了五亿美元</b><b>
a billion bucks at Goldman Sachs.</b>

21:34.370 --> 21:37.250
<b>他让雷曼兄弟倒闭? 让高盛最强的竞争对手倒闭?</b><b>
He lets Lehman die? Goldman's biggest competitor?</b>

21:37.330 --> 21:39.000
<b>那会让人怀疑他还是高盛的人呢</b><b>
Makes him look like he's still working for Goldman.</b>

21:39.090 --> 21:41.880
<b>我估计他这会儿正在财政部写支票呢</b><b>
He's just doing it out of a desk at Treasury.</b>

21:44.220 --> 21:46.090
<b>甜甜圈在哪?</b><b>
Where are the donuts?</b>

21:47.090 --> 21:49.550
<b>就是如此 若你是他们这些金融企业的首席执行官</b><b>
Exactly. If you're the CEO of one of these financial firms,</b>

21:49.640 --> 21:52.220
<b>你早就注意到政府愿意支援你收购的话</b><b>
you've already seen what the government was willing to do.</b>

21:52.310 --> 21:54.770
<b>那你可以堂而皇之地说</b><b>
Why wouldn't you play chicken with them and say,</b>

21:54.850 --> 21:58.100
<b>"当然 我们愿意协助你们 可你得给我点好处吧?</b><b>
"Sure, I'll help you out. But you gotta throw in a sweetener,</b>

21:58.190 --> 21:59.940
<b>就像你援助别人收购时所作的"</b><b>
just like you did for those guys"?</b>

22:01.400 --> 22:04.530
<b>公众以为我们会资助迪克·富尔德</b><b>
They just assume I'm gonna bail out Dick Fuld,</b>

22:04.610 --> 22:07.570
<b>以为我是那个为他们业绩不好擦屁股的人</b><b>
like I'm the guy behind the elephant with the shovel.</b>

22:07.660 --> 22:09.450
<b>公众认为雷曼兄弟这次被收购就像</b><b>
They're all drawing a line from Bear</b>

22:09.450 --> 22:11.450
<b>贝尔斯登 房利美和房地美一样</b><b>
and Fannie and Freddie right to Lehman.</b>

22:11.530 --> 22:13.370
<b>不会有纳税人再愿意支持资助另一家破产银行了</b><b>
There's no way the taxpayers are gonna go for another bailout.</b>

22:13.450 --> 22:16.080
<b>一揽子大规模收购援助政策</b><b>
Very large purchase assistance package.</b>

22:16.250 --> 22:19.330
<b>这次必须让他们自己去解决了</b><b>
We need to come up with a private-sector solution,</b>

22:19.420 --> 22:21.420
<b>让他们投行自己去弥补负债缺口</b><b>
get the investment banks to bridge the gap.</b>

22:21.500 --> 22:23.440
<b>可以 但除非他们确信您不会再</b><b>
Okay, but that's never gonna work</b>

22:23.440 --> 22:25.260
<b>支援该收购行动 否则行不通</b><b>
unless they believe that you've drawn a line.</b>

22:25.340 --> 22:28.430
<b>我知道您不喜欢向公众泄露消息 让我们和媒体交流</b><b>
I know you don't like leaking, but let us reach out to the press.</b>

22:34.890 --> 22:35.970
<b>好</b><b>
Okay.</b>

22:39.060 --> 22:41.690
<b>弗劳尔斯先生 您有电话</b><b>
Mr. Flowers, there's a call for you.</b>

22:41.770 --> 22:45.780
<b>是美国国际集团的鲍勃·维伦斯坦德 他坚持一定要与您通话</b><b>
Bob Willumstad from AIG. He's very insistent.</b>

22:49.770 --> 22:54.780
<b>罗伯特·维伦斯坦德</b>

22:49.770 --> 22:54.780
<b>美国国际集团首席执行官</b>

22:51.160 --> 22:54.620
<b>弗劳尔斯先生 我的人说你是这方面的专家</b><b>
Mr. Flowers. My people tell me you're the man to talk to.</b>

22:55.040 --> 22:56.450
<b>我们公司面临一个大问题</b><b>
We've got a real problem here.</b>

22:56.750 --> 22:58.120
<b>嗯? 什么样的问题?</b><b>
Yeah? What kind of problem?</b>

22:58.290 --> 23:01.290
<b>似乎我们的现金流就快断了</b><b>
It looks very much like we are about to run out of cash.</b>

23:01.630 --> 23:02.790
<b>美国国际集团?</b><b>
AIG?</b>

23:02.880 --> 23:04.880
<b>我们给您发了一份文件 是一份电子表格</b><b>
We've sent over a document. It's a spreadsheet.</b>

23:04.960 --> 23:07.800
<b>当然 这是一份机密文件 但会让您了解我们的困境的</b><b>
It's confidential, of course, but it might give you some insight.</b>

23:08.170 --> 23:10.470
<b>我正在处理雷曼兄弟的事情 美国银行要收购他们</b><b>
I'm in the middle of Lehman. I'm working with B of A.</b>

23:11.300 --> 23:13.470
<b>那您明天能过来一下吗?</b><b>
Is there any way you could come over tomorrow?</b>

23:13.970 --> 23:17.390
<b>我会研究下这张表 然后再说吧</b><b>
I'll take a look at the numbers and we'll talk.</b>

23:23.060 --> 23:25.230
<b>弗劳尔斯先生</b><b>
Mr. Flowers.</b>

23:28.690 --> 23:30.110
<b>谁去开下电视</b><b>
Somebody put the TV on.</b>

23:30.450 --> 23:32.860
<b>财经频道在说雷曼兄弟</b><b>
CNBC's talking about Lehman.</b>

23:37.580 --> 23:40.500
<b>一位熟悉保尔森的...</b><b>
A person familiar with Paulson's...</b>

23:40.500 --> 23:42.500
<b>一位了解财政部长汉克·保尔森想法的人透露</b><b>
Treasury Secretary Hank Paulson's thinking,</b>

23:42.580 --> 23:45.290
<b>在目前这种经济环境下</b><b>
and he is saying there will be no government money</b>

23:45.590 --> 23:47.750
<b>政府不会资助美国银行收购雷曼兄弟</b><b>
in the resolution of this situation.</b>

23:47.840 --> 23:50.170
<b>他们说雷曼兄弟被收购和贝尔斯登的情况有两处不同</b><b>
They're saying two things make the Lehman deal different.</b>

23:50.260 --> 23:52.760
<b>雷曼兄弟收购是市场早已预料到的 并有半年时间</b><b>
The market's been aware and had time to prepare</b>

23:52.840 --> 23:55.050
<b>可以准备 第二点是...</b><b>
for over six months. And the second is...</b>

23:55.140 --> 23:57.760
<b>只是电视台在胡扯?</b><b>
Is that just TV bullshit?</b>

23:57.850 --> 24:00.930
<b>还是保尔森想给我们传递的信息?</b><b>
Or is that Paulson sending us a message?</b>

24:01.690 --> 24:02.770
<b>喂 克里斯?</b><b>
Chris?</b>

24:10.360 --> 24:11.530
<b>什么? 不好意思</b><b>
Yeah? Sorry.</b>

24:15.030 --> 24:17.150
<b>"一位财政部部长的朋友"</b><b>
What exactly does "a person familiar</b>

24:17.150 --> 24:18.450
<b>这到底是什么意思?</b><b>
with the Treasury Secretary" mean?</b>

24:18.660 --> 24:20.700
<b>可能有很多的含义</b><b>
That could mean a lot of things.</b>

24:21.120 --> 24:22.460
<b>是你的某位员工胡言乱语吧?</b><b>
Did one of your staffers do this?</b>

24:22.540 --> 24:24.540
<b>一定是你十分钟前解雇了谁吧</b><b>
Please tell me someone got fired 10 minutes ago.</b>

24:24.630 --> 24:26.460
<b>那是我的意思</b><b>
The leak came from me.</b>

24:29.000 --> 24:30.380
<b>汉克 你那种公众宣言</b><b>
Hank, a public statement like that</b>

24:30.380 --> 24:32.380
<b>可能会引起很多想象不到的灾难</b><b>
can have a lot of unintended consequences.</b>

24:32.470 --> 24:34.140
<b>我们得提醒别的银行</b><b>
We had to send a message to the other banks.</b>

24:34.140 --> 24:35.340
<b>让他们自己解决了</b><b>
They need to step up.</b>

24:35.430 --> 24:37.390
<b>我的帽子里再也变不出兔子来了</b><b>
I don't have another rabbit I can pull out of my hat.</b>

24:39.310 --> 24:42.100
<b>罗基·科恩刚打电话给我</b><b>
Rodgin Cohen just called me.</b>

24:42.180 --> 24:43.440
<b>他说美国银行的收购团现在</b><b>
The B of A team is sitting there</b>

24:43.440 --> 24:44.940
<b>坐在那边在手机上玩打砖块</b><b>
playing Brickbreaker on their phones.</b>

24:45.020 --> 24:46.230
<b>他们不想收购了</b><b>
They don't want this deal.</b>

24:47.060 --> 24:49.000
<b>收购暂停是因为</b><b>
The deal is hanging by a thread because</b>

24:49.000 --> 24:50.480
<b>他们对雷曼调查得越仔细</b><b>
the closer they get to Lehman,</b>

24:50.570 --> 24:52.860
<b>就越觉得 这其实是一个废料排放场</b><b>
the more it looks like a toxic waste dump.</b>

24:53.030 --> 24:56.450
<b>所以我们得为他们收购做风险上的补偿</b><b>
Which is why at the end of the day we may have to help them,</b>

24:56.530 --> 25:00.030
<b>若您不作出那种公众宣言的话 这场收购本该是很顺利的...</b><b>
which would be a lot easier if we didn't publicly state that...</b>

25:00.120 --> 25:02.160
<b>我们不能 蒂姆! 那样做不合法!</b><b>
We can't, Tim! Legally, we can't!</b>

25:02.330 --> 25:07.580
<b>若要合法地做 那这场灾难我们也没办法阻止</b><b>
Legally, we haven't figured out how yet.</b>

25:09.090 --> 25:12.510
<b>我很担心</b><b>
I am concerned</b>

25:13.260 --> 25:18.340
<b>因为我们现在还有几种挽救措施 但我们正在</b><b>
we are limiting our options at a time when we have very few,</b>

25:18.430 --> 25:20.100
<b>浪费他们</b><b>
if any, available.</b>

25:23.100 --> 25:28.730
<b>我想让那些首席执行官聚集到一起 给他们一个周末的时间</b><b>
I want all the CEOs in a room. We've got the weekend.</b>

25:28.810 --> 25:30.900
<b>把他们关在美联储</b><b>
We lock them in a room at the Fed</b>

25:31.150 --> 25:34.570
<b>在他们自己解决雷曼兄弟这烂摊子之前 不放他们出来</b><b>
and we don't let them out until they have a solution on Lehman.</b>

25:35.110 --> 25:36.530
<b>你的燕麦粥快凉了</b><b>
Your oatmeal's getting cold.</b>

25:36.610 --> 25:39.620
<b>他们会明白事态严重性的 他们自己会掏钱的</b><b>
They'll figure it out. They'll all throw in some money.</b>

25:41.620 --> 25:44.190
<b>蒂姆强烈建议我们</b><b>
Tim is advocating strongly that we</b>

25:44.190 --> 25:45.290
<b>央行出面提供一些支援</b><b>
reconsider some kind of Fed support.</b>

25:45.540 --> 25:47.710
<b>他想让我们资助所有人</b><b>
Tim wants us to pick up the tab on everyone.</b>

25:47.710 --> 25:49.710
<b>我可不想做"破产救援大使"</b><b>
I can't be Mr. Bailout.</b>

25:50.670 --> 25:54.010
<b>而且雷曼兄弟的亏损是贝尔斯登的两倍</b><b>
The Lehman hole is twice what Bear's was.</b>

25:54.090 --> 25:55.540
<b>而且投资者正急着从中抽身出来</b><b>
Investors are pulling their accounts.</b>

25:55.540 --> 25:56.630
<b>你想长期借贷给他们吗?</b><b>
You want to lend into a run?</b>

25:58.640 --> 26:00.470
<b>那巴克莱银行呢? 他们仍想收购雷曼吗?</b><b>
What about Barclays? Are they still interested?</b>

26:00.640 --> 26:03.310
<b>他们在对待风险上比美国银行更加保守</b><b>
They can't afford the risk any more than B of A can.</b>

26:04.060 --> 26:06.810
<b>我相信你一定能够说服任何人掏出钱</b><b>
I don't doubt your ability to talk anybody into submission,</b>

26:06.890 --> 26:09.560
<b>但是这风险确实很大</b><b>
but it is still a long shot.</b>

26:09.650 --> 26:12.860
<b>而且雷曼兄弟很可能会破产</b><b>
And there's a very real possibility that Lehman goes under.</b>

26:12.940 --> 26:15.190
<b>这周将会有场收购谈判</b><b>
There's a deal to be made here.</b>

26:16.990 --> 26:18.990
<b>这场谈判一定会成功的</b><b>
I'm gonna make the deal.</b>

26:19.570 --> 26:22.830
<b>在收盘前不到一小时</b><b>
With just a little more than an hour left until the market</b>

26:22.910 --> 26:25.410
<b>雷曼兄弟的股价又猛跌了一把</b><b>
closes, shares of Lehman Brothers have taken another tumble.</b>

26:25.500 --> 26:29.580
<b>股价跌到新低 每股4美元都不到了</b><b>
The stock is now trading at a new low, under $4 a share.</b>

26:29.670 --> 26:30.980
<b>而且从卖方形势来看</b><b>
And judging from the selling,</b>

26:30.980 --> 26:34.300
<b>这种下跌趋势仍会继续</b><b>
there doesn't appear to be a bottom in sight.</b>

26:37.630 --> 26:40.130
<b>除了布兰克费恩(高盛首席执行官)说他有一场演讲 会尽量赶过来的</b><b>
So, Blankfein has a speech he's trying to get out of,</b>

26:40.220 --> 26:41.260
<b>其他的人都同意了</b><b>
but the rest have confirmed.</b>

26:41.350 --> 26:43.550
<b>- 告诉他必须来参加  - 好的</b><b>
- Tell him it's not optional.  - Yeah.</b>

26:43.810 --> 26:47.100
<b>克里斯托夫·考克斯</b>

26:43.810 --> 26:47.100
<b>美国证交会主席</b>

26:43.810 --> 26:46.100
<b>下午好 主席 欢迎来参加该次会议</b><b>
Good afternoon, Chairman. Thank you so much for joining us.</b>

26:46.810 --> 26:50.270
<b>- 这架是谁的飞机?  - 呃 这是租来的</b><b>
- Whose plane is this?  - Uh, that's a rental.</b>

26:50.350 --> 26:51.980
<b>汉克自己掏钱的</b><b>
Hank put it on his card.</b>

26:52.060 --> 26:55.020
<b>先生 你认识尼尔 这是米歇尔·戴维斯负责公众事务</b><b>
Sir, you know Neel and Michele Davis, Public Affairs.</b>

26:55.110 --> 26:56.150
<b>嗨 很高兴见面</b><b>
Hi. Pleasure.</b>

26:56.240 --> 26:58.440
<b>- 这位是丹·杰斯特 我们团队的新人  - 你好</b><b>
- This is Dan Jester, our new numbers guy.  - Hi.</b>

26:58.530 --> 27:00.280
<b>是我劝他退休后继续出来工作的</b><b>
I talked him into coming out of retirement.</b>

27:00.360 --> 27:02.870
<b>- 什么? 退休?  - 我们以前在高盛是同事</b><b>
- Excuse me? Retirement?  - He was with us at Goldman.</b>

27:03.080 --> 27:05.240
<b>财政部还有没有员工不是从高盛过来的?</b><b>
Got anybody at Treasury who wasn't at Goldman?</b>

27:05.330 --> 27:06.200
<b>主席 有一点必须澄清一下</b><b>
Chairman, just to be clear,</b>

27:06.200 --> 27:09.000
<b>我们财政部和高盛之间没有任何利益冲突</b><b>
there's no question of conflict of interest.</b>

27:09.080 --> 27:11.790
<b>汉克在任职前就将高盛所有的股份抛售了</b><b>
Hank sold all of his Goldman stock before he took office.</b>

27:11.880 --> 27:14.210
<b>- 我什么也没暗示  - 不好意思</b><b>
- I wasn't implying anything.  - Sorry.</b>

27:14.300 --> 27:17.380
<b>我们对外面所传的"高盛政府"的谣言比较敏感</b><b>
We're a little touchy about the whole "Government Sachs" thing.</b>

27:18.050 --> 27:19.840
<b>我们走吧?</b><b>
Shall we?</b>

27:23.430 --> 27:25.510
<b>美国银行发现雷曼的不良资产越来越多</b><b>
B of A keeps finding more toxic assets.</b>

27:25.510 --> 27:27.810
<b>他们需要政府介入模仿之前摩根大通的收购</b><b>
They want you to reconsider a Jamie deal.</b>

27:27.890 --> 27:29.480
<b>他们会承担10亿元的损失</b><b>
They'll split the first billion in losses,</b>

27:29.480 --> 27:31.480
<b>剩余的40亿损失的由政府提供担保</b><b>
but they want you on the hook for the next 40.</b>

27:31.560 --> 27:32.850
<b>就像你对贝尔斯登收购做的一样</b><b>
You did it for Bear.</b>

27:34.150 --> 27:35.940
<b>葛瑞格 我过会打给你</b><b>
Greg, let me get back to you.</b>

27:36.400 --> 27:38.690
<b>难道我得在我额头上纹个字才行吗?</b><b>
What, do I have to tattoo it on my forehead?</b>

27:38.690 --> 27:39.990
<b>我们不会对雷曼兄弟收购提供一分钱</b><b>
We are not bailing out Lehman.</b>

27:40.070 --> 27:41.650
<b>这是华尔街自己赌博失败</b><b>
Wall Street has a gambling problem.</b>

27:41.740 --> 27:44.530
<b>若老是让政府为他们擦屁股</b><b>
If government keeps covering their losses,</b>

27:44.530 --> 27:45.830
<b>他们永远也得不到教训</b><b>
they never learn anything.</b>

27:47.700 --> 27:49.450
<b>- 怎么了?  - 我不知道您是想继续</b><b>
- What?  - I didn't know if you wanted</b>

27:49.460 --> 27:51.530
<b>教导我道德危机</b><b>
to keep lecturing me on moral hazard</b>

27:51.530 --> 27:53.830
<b>还是想让我拒绝美国银行提议</b><b>
or if I should just call B of A back.</b>

27:54.540 --> 27:55.550
<b>我们只能让他们都坐在一起 进行讨论</b><b>
We need to keep them at the table</b>

27:55.560 --> 27:57.750
<b>直到这些企业找到自己的解决方法</b><b>
until they come up with a private-sector solution.</b>

27:57.840 --> 27:59.420
<b>告诉他们最好照我说的做</b><b>
Tell them to stay with us.</b>

28:01.090 --> 28:02.880
<b>- 阿利斯泰尔 你好啊  - 你好 Henry</b><b>
- Alistair, hello.  - Hello, Henry.</b>

28:02.970 --> 28:05.090
<b>请等一下</b><b>
Hold on one second.</b>

28:06.600 --> 28:08.560
<b>英国财政大臣打来的</b><b>
Chancellor of the Exchequer.</b>

28:08.640 --> 28:12.020
<b>我了解到巴克莱银行想收购雷曼兄弟</b><b>
I understand Barclays is one of your potential buyers for Lehman.</b>

28:12.100 --> 28:14.810
<b>但我国的银行最近的资金压力也很大</b><b>
My banks are already under a great deal of stress.</b>

28:14.900 --> 28:16.610
<b>我可不想承担过多义务</b><b>
I don't want to become overextended.</b>

28:16.690 --> 28:19.150
<b>雷曼兄弟虽然最近出了问题 但还是有价值的</b><b>
Lehman is problematic, but there's value there.</b>

28:19.230 --> 28:23.450
<b>我们会让他能够盈利的 继续保持合作吧</b><b>
We will find a way to make it attractive. Just stay with us.</b>

28:23.950 --> 28:25.110
<b>那再说吧</b><b>
Talk soon then.</b>

28:25.200 --> 28:26.450
<b>再见</b><b>
Bye.</b>

28:26.660 --> 28:30.560
<b>2008年9月18日,星期五</b>

28:26.660 --> 28:31.160
<b>我们不会拒绝巴克莱银行 但最好还是由美国银行来收购</b><b>
We'll keep Barclays in the mix, but B of A is still our best bet.</b>

28:31.660 --> 28:35.210
<b>我们今晚会召集所有主要银行的首席执行官过来开会</b><b>
We've got the CEOs of every major bank coming here tonight.</b>

28:35.290 --> 28:38.340
<b>我们得明白地告诉他们 这是他们自己捅的篓子</b><b>
We have to make it clear that this is their problem,</b>

28:38.420 --> 28:41.840
<b>我们政府可以做顾问或是盟友</b><b>
that we are their advisors and their allies,</b>

28:41.920 --> 28:45.970
<b>但我们不是他们的保险箱</b><b>
but we are not their safety net.</b>

28:47.140 --> 28:48.470
<b>对这些人 我们还能指望什么呢?</b><b>
What should we expect from these guys?</b>

28:51.840 --> 28:54.300
<b>美联储·纽约</b>

28:59.440 --> 29:01.230
<b>杰米很聪明</b><b>
Jamie is smart.</b>

29:01.320 --> 29:04.450
<b>他买下贝尔斯登后 手头可运作的资金就不多了</b><b>
He doesn't have as much cash to work with since he bought Bear.</b>

29:01.470 --> 29:05.450
<b>杰米·戴蒙</b>

29:01.470 --> 29:05.450
<b>摩根大通主席兼首席执行官</b>

29:06.870 --> 29:08.740
<b>劳埃德是巨星</b><b>
Lloyd's a superstar.</b>

29:09.870 --> 29:11.700
<b>高盛是华尔街上最精明的一家</b><b>
Goldman's the smartest shop on the Block.</b>

29:11.790 --> 29:15.160
<b>虽然我之前当过他老板 但那并不表示 他就会听我的了</b><b>
And just because I used to be his boss, it doesn't mean he's gonna listen to me.</b>

29:14.180 --> 29:16.600
<b>劳埃德·布兰克费恩</b>

29:14.180 --> 29:16.600
<b>高盛主席兼首席执行官</b>

29:17.250 --> 29:20.090
<b>约翰·麦克 他过去常常满楼层东奔西跑 大呼小叫</b><b>
John Mack, he used to run around the floor screaming,</b>

29:20.170 --> 29:23.510
<b>"水里有血啊! 我们杀啊!"</b><b>
"There's blood in the water! Let's go kill someone!"</b>

29:24.260 --> 29:26.340
<b>他是好战分子</b><b>
He's a fighter.</b>

29:26.370 --> 29:28.000
<b>约翰·麦克</b>

29:26.370 --> 29:28.000
<b>摩根士丹利主席兼首席执行官</b>

29:28.220 --> 29:32.010
<b>塞恩是我在高盛的副手 他很自私 是个实用主义者</b><b>
Thain was my number two at Goldman. He's selfish. He's a pragmatist.</b>

29:32.100 --> 29:35.350
<b>他知道 如果雷曼兄弟倒了 下一个就轮到美林证券了</b><b>
He knows if Lehman goes, Merrill's next.</b>

29:33.360 --> 29:36.300
<b>约翰·塞恩</b>

29:33.360 --> 29:36.300
<b>美林证券主席兼首席执行官</b>

29:37.350 --> 29:40.360
<b>维克拉姆·潘迪特刚入职花旗</b><b>
Vikram Pandit is the new guy at Citigroup.</b>

29:41.940 --> 29:45.530
<b>没人知道 是他在运作花旗 还是花旗在运作他</b><b>
No one knows if he's running Citi or if Citi's running him.</b>

29:42.540 --> 29:45.800
<b>维克拉姆·潘迪特</b>

29:42.540 --> 29:45.800
<b>花旗集团首席执行官</b>

30:08.720 --> 30:11.890
<b>感谢各位匆忙之中赶来这里</b><b>
Thanks for coming down here on such short notice.</b>

30:12.810 --> 30:16.600
<b>下周一早上 雷曼兄弟将无法偿付其债务</b><b>
Monday morning, Lehman will no longer be able to honor its obligations.</b>

30:19.400 --> 30:22.230
<b>有两家有意购买 美国银行和巴克莱银行</b><b>
We have two potential buyers. B of A and Barclays.</b>

30:22.320 --> 30:26.820
<b>但如果没有第三方融资 它们都无法完成收购</b><b>
Neither will take the company unless someone else finances part of the deal.</b>

30:26.900 --> 30:30.200
<b>政府不会进行干预</b><b>
The government is not in a position to step in.</b>

30:31.490 --> 30:34.580
<b>上一次是最后一次 这次就由你们完成了</b><b>
I did the last one. You're gonna do this one.</b>

30:34.700 --> 30:36.040
<b>迪克·富尔德在哪儿?</b><b>
Where's Dick Fuld?</b>

30:36.120 --> 30:38.370
<b>迪克不适合再做决定了</b><b>
Dick's in no condition to make any decisions.</b>

30:38.460 --> 30:41.460
<b>我们将各位分成三组</b><b>
We're breaking you into three groups.</b>

30:41.750 --> 30:46.380
<b>第一组 评估雷曼兄弟的不良资产</b><b>
The first one will try to value Lehman's toxic assets.</b>

30:46.760 --> 30:49.970
<b>第二组 设计投资架构 让大家都可以投资雷曼</b><b>
The second one will work on some sort of structure for you all to invest in Lehman.</b>

30:50.390 --> 30:54.010
<b>第三组 制定熄灯计划</b><b>
And the third one works on the lights-out plan.</b>

30:54.350 --> 30:56.600
<b>如果雷曼兄弟申请破产 我们需要考虑</b><b>
If Lehman files for bankruptcy, we need to figure out</b>

30:56.680 --> 30:58.890
<b>如何遏制对各家的损害</b><b>
how to contain the damage to the rest of you.</b>

30:59.190 --> 31:00.270
<b>天呐</b><b>
Christ.</b>

31:00.440 --> 31:02.150
<b>我们早就预见到会出现这种状况</b><b>
We've all seen this coming for miles.</b>

31:02.230 --> 31:05.360
<b>我认为 雷曼兄弟即使破产 也不会给我们公司带来太大影响</b><b>
I don't think a Lehman bankruptcy takes down our firms.</b>

31:05.440 --> 31:07.940
<b>所以呢 我们就只能祝福雷曼了吗?</b><b>
What, are we crossing our fingers?</b>

31:08.110 --> 31:13.120
<b>这是要求我们挽救竞争对手 别表现得好像在帮我们一样</b><b>
You're asking us to save a competitor. Let's not act like you're doing us a favor.</b>

31:13.660 --> 31:17.370
<b>各位 各位 大家都是伟大的美国人</b><b>
Gentlemen, gentlemen, you are great Americans</b>

31:17.450 --> 31:19.330
<b>这是承担我们的爱国责任</b><b>
undertaking a patriotic duty.</b>

31:19.830 --> 31:22.960
<b>各位的努力将为自身赢得</b><b>
Your travail will earn you the love</b>

31:23.210 --> 31:25.460
<b>举国的爱戴和感激</b><b>
and gratitude of your country.</b>

31:25.710 --> 31:27.800
<b>我记得 托马斯·潘恩(激进民主主义者)曾经说过 "这些..."</b><b>
I think it was Thomas Paine who said, "These are..."</b>

31:27.880 --> 31:30.090
<b>雷曼兄弟是在座各家银行的合作伙伴</b><b>
Lehman is a trading partner for every bank in this room.</b>

31:30.180 --> 31:32.890
<b>它的破产将对大家都有很大冲击</b><b>
Their failure will be a massive blow to all of you.</b>

31:32.970 --> 31:34.510
<b>这就是重点</b><b>
This is your problem.</b>

31:34.680 --> 31:37.560
<b>我们可以好好说说 为何会到如此地步</b><b>
We can all argue about how we got here.</b>

31:37.640 --> 31:41.230
<b>放松管制 衍生品 迪克·富尔德决策不利</b><b>
Deregulation, derivatives, Dick Fuld made bad decisions.</b>

31:41.600 --> 31:44.810
<b>我们都有责任 这是灾难性的动荡</b><b>
We're all responsible. It's a catastrophic mess.</b>

31:45.730 --> 31:48.650
<b>政府已经竭尽所能 现在全靠你们了</b><b>
The government's done whatever it can do. It's on you now.</b>

31:49.110 --> 31:51.490
<b>各位该解决问题 付出代价了</b><b>
You need to fix it and you need to pay for it.</b>

31:51.740 --> 31:53.700
<b>我就直说了</b><b>
Let me be clear.</b>

31:54.990 --> 31:59.500
<b>没出力的人 我们会记下的</b><b>
We will remember anyone who is not helpful.</b>

32:07.990 --> 32:16.000
<b>2008年9月13日,星期六</b>

32:23.270 --> 32:25.100
<b>你注意到这其中的小规律了吗?</b><b>
Do you notice a little pattern here?</b>

32:25.190 --> 32:27.940
<b>不见棺材不掉泪</b><b>
We don't deal with things until there's some kind of emergency on the table.</b>

32:28.030 --> 32:30.110
<b>是啊 不到最后一刻 没人会去处理的</b><b>
Yeah, we don't deal with things until Friday.</b>

32:30.190 --> 32:31.320
<b>现在一只脚已经踏进去了</b><b>
Some kind of a weekend thing.</b>

32:31.400 --> 32:32.450
<b>我们什么时候才能</b><b>
When were we gonna figure out</b>

32:32.530 --> 32:34.610
<b>找到解决投资银行的破产问题的好方法?</b><b>
exactly how to handle the failure of an investment bank?</b>

32:34.700 --> 32:36.320
<b>周末搞定吧</b><b>
Let's do it over a weekend.</b>

32:36.410 --> 32:39.790
<b>我刚刚跟一位密切关注现状的专家谈过</b><b>
I talked to a person who is monitoring the situation out there,</b>

32:39.870 --> 32:44.000
<b>他说 业界人士都期望 他们能和杰米·戴蒙一样 得到政府的自助</b><b>
and the person said they all want the same deal Jamie Dimon got,</b>

32:44.080 --> 32:46.130
<b>但预计期望会落空</b><b>
and they're not going to get it.</b>

32:46.290 --> 32:49.380
<b>提醒一句 克里斯·弗劳尔斯正在大厅</b><b>
Just a heads up, Chris Flowers is in the lobby.</b>

32:49.460 --> 32:52.380
<b>他是美国银行收购雷曼案的顾问</b><b>
He's consulting for B of A on Lehman.</b>

32:53.720 --> 32:56.180
<b>汉克之前将弗劳尔斯挤出了高盛</b><b>
Hank pushed Flowers out of Goldman.</b>

32:56.260 --> 32:59.890
<b>昨天我们还认为雷曼的不良资产仅300亿 今天就涨到了700亿</b><b>
Yesterday, we thought Lehman was holding 30 billion in crap. Today it's 70.</b>

33:00.020 --> 33:03.390
<b>700亿不良资产 这还只是随机抽样</b><b>
$70 billion in assets that we're valuing with a dartboard.</b>

33:03.480 --> 33:04.730
<b>没事 我们会解决这个问题</b><b>
No, we're gonna work this out.</b>

33:05.060 --> 33:07.310
<b>除非政府干预 不然我们就停手</b><b>
Unless you step in, we're ending this.</b>

33:07.400 --> 33:08.690
<b>别忘了迪克</b><b>
Don't forget about Dick.</b>

33:08.770 --> 33:12.740
<b>好了 迪克·富尔德不停打来电话 不停要求我们提高价格</b><b>
Yeah, Dick Fuld keeps calling, hammering us to raise the price.</b>

33:14.860 --> 33:16.860
<b>抱歉</b><b>
Excuse me.</b>

33:20.490 --> 33:25.370
<b>700亿不良资产 还无担保?</b><b>
70 fucking billion and no collateral?</b>

33:27.420 --> 33:29.590
<b>如果雷曼兄弟本周末破产</b><b>
If Lehman Brothers fails this weekend,</b>

33:29.670 --> 33:33.920
<b>专家们毫不怀疑 下一个将是美林证券</b><b>
there's little doubt amongst the people I speak to that Merrill Lynch will be next.</b>

33:34.010 --> 33:36.180
<b>信心是非常脆弱的</b><b>
Confidence is a very fragile thing.</b>

33:36.260 --> 33:39.930
<b>在金融市场里 信心的流失速度非常快</b><b>
And in our financial markets, it is eroding very quickly.</b>

33:40.010 --> 33:45.100
<b>雷曼撑不下去了 我们就是下一个 必须立刻采取措施了</b><b>
Lehman's not gonna make it. We're next. We need to do something right now.</b>

33:45.480 --> 33:48.770
<b>只有美国银行能救我们了 我可以打个电话看看</b><b>
B of A's the only one out there. I can put in a call.</b>

33:48.860 --> 33:50.940
<b>- 虽然这样会毁了雷曼 不过...  - 雷曼是自食其果</b><b>
- It screws Lehman, but...  - Lehman screwed themselves.</b>

33:51.020 --> 33:56.530
<b>保尔森已经划定了底线 雷曼完了 打电话吧</b><b>
Paulson has drawn a line in the sand. Lehman is dead. Make the call.</b>

33:59.780 --> 34:03.120
<b>你们考虑一下收购美林的股份吧</b><b>
We'd like you guys to look at taking a stake in Merrill,</b>

34:03.200 --> 34:05.960
<b>有约10%的利润</b><b>
something in the neighborhood of 10%.</b>

34:06.120 --> 34:09.790
<b>我不知道能否拿到10%的利润</b><b>
I don't know if I can generate any interest in 10%,</b>

34:10.630 --> 34:13.590
<b>不过如果是收购整家公司的话</b><b>
but if the whole company's in play,</b>

34:13.670 --> 34:15.800
<b>我们肯定是愿意考虑一下的</b><b>
I bet that's something that we'd consider.</b>

34:15.970 --> 34:17.930
<b>我们和雷曼?</b><b>
Us and Lehman?</b>

34:18.840 --> 34:20.720
<b>这种规模的收购 我们只能完成一家</b><b>
Deal this size, there's only room for one.</b>

34:27.560 --> 34:32.480
<b>毫无疑问 风险很大 但是只要各位不中途退出</b><b>
It is a lot of risk, no question, but if you stay in the game,</b>

34:32.570 --> 34:34.980
<b>- 就都能找到各自的解决之道  - 当然了</b><b>
- we all will find a private solution.  - Absolutely.</b>

34:37.280 --> 34:41.660
<b>别被这些数字吓到了 我们会解决的 雷曼是值得收购的</b><b>
Don't get scared by the numbers. We'll figure it out. Lehman is worth owning.</b>

34:41.740 --> 34:44.450
<b>各位 有空吗?</b><b>
Guys, you got a second?</b>

34:48.040 --> 34:49.920
<b>我昨天去过了美国国际集团</b><b>
I was at AIG yesterday.</b>

34:50.000 --> 34:54.590
<b>下周三 他们将有至少50亿的缺口</b><b>
Next Wednesday, they got a $5 billion hole, minimum.</b>

34:55.760 --> 34:59.510
<b>我跟沃伦·巴菲特联系过了 他表示绝对不会帮忙</b><b>
I called Warren Buffett. He wouldn't touch it with a stick.</b>

35:00.680 --> 35:01.930
<b>我们会调查清楚</b><b>
We're looking into it.</b>

35:02.010 --> 35:03.970
<b>这是一家非常大的公司</b><b>
It's a very big company.</b>

35:06.350 --> 35:10.350
<b>谢了 克里斯 感谢你所有的帮助</b><b>
Thanks, Chris. I appreciate all your help.</b>

35:17.530 --> 35:19.530
<b>他们根本不了解状况</b><b>
They're not on top of it.</b>

35:26.290 --> 35:28.370
<b>看看这个</b><b>
Look at this.</b>

35:31.920 --> 35:34.420
<b>这可能吗?</b><b>
Is this even possible?</b>

35:34.920 --> 35:36.250
<b>美国国际集团?</b><b>
AIG?</b>

35:36.550 --> 35:37.590
<b>该死的</b><b>
Holy shit.</b>

35:39.550 --> 35:41.130
<b>调查清楚</b><b>
Get into this.</b>

35:43.470 --> 35:44.510
<b>嘿 约翰</b><b>
John.</b>

35:50.190 --> 35:52.770
<b>你明白现在的状况吗?</b><b>
Do you see what's happening here?</b>

35:53.560 --> 35:55.440
<b>你想好怎么为自己打算了吗?</b><b>
Are you watching out for yourself?</b>

35:55.520 --> 35:59.990
<b>我不笨 我正在采取行动</b><b>
I'm not thick. I'm working on something.</b>

36:03.620 --> 36:05.990
<b>你想去找美国银行</b><b>
You're talking to B of A.</b>

36:07.990 --> 36:09.330
<b>抱歉</b><b>
I'm sorry.</b>

36:10.370 --> 36:12.920
<b>我知道 这样对雷曼不好 但是我必须先顾好美林</b><b>
I know it's not good for Lehman, but I have to take care of Merrill.</b>

36:13.080 --> 36:15.460
<b>把雷曼扔给我来操心</b><b>
Let me worry about Lehman.</b>

36:16.420 --> 36:19.130
<b>巴克莱还没有退出</b><b>
Barclays is still in the game.</b>

36:21.470 --> 36:22.590
<b>你去搞定吧</b><b>
Just get it done.</b>

36:33.850 --> 36:37.360
<b>美国银行将收购美林</b><b>
B of A is gonna buy Merrill.</b>

36:39.900 --> 36:41.690
<b>我们必须让巴克莱出手</b><b>
We need to make Barclays work.</b>

36:43.030 --> 36:45.320
<b>我记得你说过 英国佬只说不做的</b><b>
I thought you said the British never close.</b>

36:46.030 --> 36:49.910
<b>他们就在外面 似乎真的很想收购</b><b>
They're here. They seem to really want it.</b>

36:50.000 --> 36:53.210
<b>只要我们主动一点 他们就会收购的</b><b>
If we hold their hands, they'll close.</b>

36:53.290 --> 36:58.670
<b>罗基 怎么回事? 盖特纳不接电话 保尔森也不接电话</b><b>
Rodgin, what the fuck? I can't get Geithner. I can't get Paulson.</b>

36:58.750 --> 37:01.590
<b>连我的手下现在也不接电话了</b><b>
I can't even get my own goddamn employees to pick up the phone.</b>

37:01.670 --> 37:03.630
<b>迪克 大家都太忙了</b><b>
There's a lot happening down here, Dick.</b>

37:03.720 --> 37:05.130
<b>噢 该死</b><b>
Oh, fuck.</b>

37:05.720 --> 37:07.930
<b>给我听好 你去告诉盖特纳</b><b>
You know what? You tell Geithner,</b>

37:08.010 --> 37:11.060
<b>他要是不帮我把这事解决了 下一个就轮到美林了</b><b>
he doesn't pull my ass out of the fire, Merrill's gonna be next.</b>

37:11.180 --> 37:12.310
<b>他知道</b><b>
He knows that.</b>

37:12.390 --> 37:16.770
<b>迪克 他刚告诉我 他们正在为美林寻找出路</b><b>
Dick, he just told me they're working on a solution for Merrill.</b>

37:20.190 --> 37:22.150
<b>那群混蛋要去帮美林?</b><b>
Those cocksuckers are gonna bail out Merrill?</b>

37:22.240 --> 37:23.820
<b>不 不是美联储</b><b>
No, no, not the Fed.</b>

37:24.110 --> 37:27.870
<b>没有私营买家了 只有美国银行和...</b><b>
There's no private buyers. There's just B of A and...</b>

37:29.450 --> 37:31.490
<b>他们想让美国银行收购美林?</b><b>
They're gonna put B of A together with Merrill?</b>

37:31.580 --> 37:34.080
<b>还有巴克莱银行 汉克觉得...</b><b>
We still have Barclays. Hank feels that...</b>

37:34.160 --> 37:37.960
<b>联邦政府竟然给我帮倒忙?</b><b>
The federal government is snaking my deal?</b>

37:39.290 --> 37:41.800
<b>我简直不敢相信!</b><b>
I cannot fucking believe this shit!</b>

37:44.470 --> 37:46.220
<b>美国银行和美林达成协议了?</b><b>
B of A made a deal with Merrill?</b>

37:46.300 --> 37:48.300
<b>对 雷曼的问题还是没解决</b><b>
Yeah, Lehman's still our problem.</b>

37:47.320 --> 37:51.000
<b>2008年9月14日,星期天</b>

37:49.010 --> 37:51.140
<b>再来这么一次 我可受不了了</b><b>
I don't think I can take another day of this.</b>

37:51.220 --> 37:54.520
<b>你是刚下梅赛德斯 来到纽约美联储</b><b>
You're getting out of a Mercedes to go to the New York Federal Reserve.</b>

37:54.600 --> 37:57.310
<b>可不是奥马哈海滩的希金斯快艇</b><b>
It's not a Higgins boat on Omaha Beach.</b>

38:06.030 --> 38:08.780
<b>好了 好了 时间已经够长了</b><b>
Okay, okay, we've been here a long time.</b>

38:09.870 --> 38:12.120
<b>别废话了</b><b>
Let's stop fucking around.</b>

38:12.200 --> 38:15.120
<b>政府想让华尔街付账</b><b>
Main Street wants Wall Street to pay.</b>

38:15.210 --> 38:18.040
<b>他们觉得 我们就是有钱的笨蛋</b><b>
They think we're overpaid assholes.</b>

38:19.040 --> 38:21.590
<b>没有哪条政策规定 一定要参与紧急援助</b><b>
There's no politician who's gonna sign off on a bailout.</b>

38:21.670 --> 38:25.590
<b>那为什么不去资助那些赚钱的人呢?</b><b>
Why would you bail out people whose sole job is to make money?</b>

38:25.670 --> 38:29.590
<b>简单点说一下现在的状况吧</b><b>
So, let's make this real simple.</b>

38:30.600 --> 38:34.470
<b>汉克认为 他可以把雷曼好的资产出售给巴克莱银行</b><b>
Hank thinks he can sell the good parts of Lehman to Barclays,</b>

38:34.560 --> 38:38.890
<b>但这样就得有人把拖垮这家公司的抵押房产接手下来</b><b>
but someone has to take the real estate crap that's weighing down the company.</b>

38:38.980 --> 38:40.730
<b>谁都不知道这些不良资产的价值</b><b>
Nobody knows how much this shit is worth,</b>

38:40.810 --> 38:42.940
<b>但我们很清楚 一定得有人买下这批资产 以完成收购</b><b>
but we know somebody has to buy it to make a deal.</b>

38:43.400 --> 38:47.280
<b>我不喜欢这样 没人喜欢这样</b><b>
I don't like it. Nobody likes it.</b>

38:47.820 --> 38:50.240
<b>那就别抱怨了 去做吧</b><b>
Let's just suck it up and do it.</b>

38:50.620 --> 38:56.000
<b>有多少人可以投个10亿元 阻止雷曼的颓势?</b><b>
How many of you can kick in a billion dollars to stop Lehman from going down?</b>

38:58.920 --> 39:01.500
<b>我投 10亿</b><b>
I'm in. One billion.</b>

39:14.010 --> 39:16.180
<b>好</b><b>
Okay.</b>

39:21.480 --> 39:24.230
<b>高盛投10亿</b><b>
Goldman's in for a billion.</b>

39:31.570 --> 39:32.990
<b>约翰 你呢?</b><b>
John?</b>

39:34.280 --> 39:35.410
<b>喂?</b><b>
Yeah?</b>

39:41.420 --> 39:42.460
<b>是</b><b>
Yes.</b>

39:45.050 --> 39:46.130
<b>好</b><b>
Yeah.</b>

39:49.260 --> 39:50.300
<b>是</b><b>
Yes.</b>

39:55.640 --> 39:57.890
<b>成功了 巴克莱银行愿意购买</b><b>
We did it. Barclays came through.</b>

39:58.140 --> 39:59.810
<b>太棒了!</b><b>
Too goddamn right!</b>

39:59.890 --> 40:04.440
<b>巴克莱不愿意要不动产资产 但是其他银行同意收购这部分了</b><b>
Barclays won't touch the real estate assets, but the other banks agreed to cover those.</b>

40:06.480 --> 40:10.320
<b>通知董事会 把大家都喊来 我们有交易要谈了</b><b>
Call the board. Get everybody here. We got a deal to make.</b>

40:10.530 --> 40:11.700
<b>好的</b><b>
Okay.</b>

40:19.000 --> 40:23.000
<b>伦敦,晚上9点</b>

40:21.920 --> 40:23.000
<b>找到他了吗?</b><b>
Did you get him?</b>

40:23.080 --> 40:25.500
<b>盖特纳不回我电话</b><b>
Geithner doesn't return my calls.</b>

40:26.340 --> 40:27.960
<b>我们一个人都找不到</b><b>
We can't get hold of any of those people.</b>

40:28.050 --> 40:30.920
<b>今天之前 没有我们发话 他们是签不了协议的</b><b>
At the end of the day, they can't sign the deal without our say-so.</b>

40:31.010 --> 40:33.130
<b>对 但是他们知道吗?</b><b>
Yes, but do they know that?</b>

40:36.760 --> 40:42.890
<b>卡勒姆·麦卡锡爵士</b>

40:36.760 --> 40:42.890
<b>英国银监会主席</b>

40:36.760 --> 40:37.890
<b>对</b><b>
Yes.</b>

40:38.810 --> 40:42.680
<b>嗯 一定 既然他屈尊来电 那就放他一马吧</b><b>
Yes, by all means, now that he deigns to call, put him through.</b>

40:43.020 --> 40:45.690
<b>卡勒姆爵士 抱歉没能回电</b><b>
Sir Callum, sorry I haven't gotten back to you.</b>

40:45.770 --> 40:49.360
<b>我们在处理巴克莱银行收购雷曼的事宜</b><b>
We're just sorting through this Barclays deal for Lehman.</b>

40:50.360 --> 40:52.490
<b>身为巴克莱银行的监管方</b><b>
As Barclays' regulator,</b>

40:52.570 --> 40:55.490
<b>我们非常关注这桩计划中的交易</b><b>
we have serious concerns about this proposed arrangement.</b>

40:55.570 --> 40:59.450
<b>什么? 你是说你不同意这桩交易?</b><b>
What? Are you saying you won't approve the deal?</b>

40:59.540 --> 41:03.000
<b>就算我们同意这桩交易 事实上并非如此</b><b>
Even if we were comfortable with the agreement, which we are not,</b>

41:03.080 --> 41:07.080
<b>巴克莱银行也需要至少提前30天征得股东同意</b><b>
Barclays would need at least 30 days for shareholder approval.</b>

41:07.170 --> 41:11.880
<b>不 不 不 他不能 他不能这样做</b><b>
No, no, no, no, no, no. He can't. He can't do this.</b>

41:11.970 --> 41:14.630
<b>- 他们能阻止交易吗?  - 是的 当然可以了</b><b>
- Can they stop the deal?  - Yeah, of course they can stop the deal.</b>

41:14.720 --> 41:16.640
<b>不过就算他们阻止不了 光是耽搁一下 雷曼也完了</b><b>
But even if they don't stop it, the delay will kill it.</b>

41:16.720 --> 41:20.180
<b>立刻给英国财政大臣打电话</b><b>
Let's call the Chancellor of the Exchequer right now.</b>

41:20.390 --> 41:25.190
<b>巴克莱银行绝对不会接受任何不良资产</b><b>
None of those assets would be part of Barclays.</b>

41:26.310 --> 41:30.520
<b>是 但是如果英国金融服务管理局要...</b><b>
Yes, but if the FSA were to...</b>

41:31.030 --> 41:32.280
<b>我们需要稳定的局势</b><b>
We need stability.</b>

41:32.360 --> 41:35.070
<b>当然</b><b>
Of course.</b>

41:35.160 --> 41:38.030
<b>对英国金融系统而言 它也是 你们肯定发现了</b><b>
must be to the British financial system. Surely you see that.</b>

41:38.120 --> 41:39.240
<b>当然</b><b>
Yeah.</b>

41:39.870 --> 41:42.240
<b>晚安 好运</b><b>
I wish you good night and good luck.</b>

41:43.410 --> 41:45.580
<b>晚安</b><b>
Good night to you, too.</b>

41:53.300 --> 41:55.760
<b>"我们不会引入你们的癌症"</b><b>
"We don't want to import your cancer."</b>

42:08.350 --> 42:09.770
<b>各位</b><b>
Those of you</b>

42:11.230 --> 42:14.360
<b>不想帮助巴克莱收购案的人</b><b>
who didn't want to assist the Barclays deal,</b>

42:14.440 --> 42:17.110
<b>现在可以松一口气了</b><b>
you can breathe a sigh of relief.</b>

42:18.320 --> 42:19.410
<b>交易取消</b><b>
The deal's not gonna happen.</b>

42:19.490 --> 42:21.740
<b>- 嘿 我们筹到钱了  - 交易没了</b><b>
- Hey, we have the money.  - Deal's dead.</b>

42:22.740 --> 42:25.120
<b>巴克莱的监管方不愿签字</b><b>
British regulator won't sign off.</b>

42:25.210 --> 42:26.790
<b>你们可以施压啊</b><b>
There must be some pressure you can exert.</b>

42:26.870 --> 42:29.460
<b>相信我 我已经尽力了</b><b>
Trust me, I've done everything I can.</b>

42:29.790 --> 42:31.210
<b>英国佬</b><b>
The British,</b>

42:33.300 --> 42:35.260
<b>耍了我们</b><b>
they grin-fucked us.</b>

42:38.550 --> 42:42.220
<b>保尔森有10万雇员 盖特纳有200名律师</b><b>
Paulson's got 100,000 employees. Geithner has 200 lawyers.</b>

42:42.310 --> 42:44.720
<b>该死的克里斯·考克斯有3千手下</b><b>
Frigging Chris Cox has 3,000 people.</b>

42:44.810 --> 42:47.520
<b>这群混蛋就没一个人拿起话筒</b><b>
Not a single one of those assholes could pick up a phone,</b>

42:47.600 --> 42:50.100
<b>给英国佬打电话 趁他们还没在周末剥削完我们的资金前</b><b>
call the British, find out if there was a deal to be made</b>

42:50.190 --> 42:53.860
<b>看看能不能搞定这桩交易?</b><b>
before they spend the weekend sweating us for cash?</b>

42:53.940 --> 42:55.280
<b>有人失误了</b><b>
Somebody dropped the ball.</b>

42:55.360 --> 42:57.190
<b>他们不是失误</b><b>
They didn't drop the ball.</b>

42:57.280 --> 42:59.070
<b>是有意犯错 激怒高管</b><b>
They dropped the ball, kicked the coach in the nuts</b>

42:59.160 --> 43:01.200
<b>故意把事情搞得一团糟</b><b>
and took a crap in the quarterback's mouth.</b>

43:01.280 --> 43:02.820
<b>当然</b><b>
Of course.</b>

43:05.790 --> 43:07.910
<b>联邦政府会有所行动</b><b>
The Fed will do something.</b>

43:09.120 --> 43:10.290
<b>必须的</b><b>
They have to.</b>

43:15.380 --> 43:17.130
<b>我们要马上对外宣布 雷曼破产的消息</b><b>
We've got to announce the Lehman bankruptcy now.</b>

43:17.220 --> 43:20.840
<b>如果亚洲股市开盘 收购案还没敲定 大家都要做最坏的打算</b><b>
If Asia opens and this isn't locked down, everyone's gonna assume the worst.</b>

43:20.930 --> 43:23.140
<b>证券跌价会导致美国银行收购美林的失败</b><b>
The sell-off will kill the Merrill-B of A deal.</b>

43:23.220 --> 43:25.600
<b>- 谁去发布公告?  - 我想应该有美国证监会来</b><b>
- Who's gonna make the announcement?  - I think it's gotta be SEC.</b>

43:25.680 --> 43:26.810
<b>对</b><b>
Yeah.</b>

43:28.730 --> 43:29.850
<b>好</b><b>
Okay.</b>

43:33.190 --> 43:35.320
<b>那就决定了 什么时候开始行动?</b><b>
Let's do it here. How soon can we set that up?</b>

43:35.400 --> 43:36.730
<b>现在</b><b>
Right away.</b>

43:36.820 --> 43:39.530
<b>我们可以用主楼层 门厅那里</b><b>
We could use the main floor, the entrance hall.</b>

43:39.610 --> 43:42.160
<b>我后面还能有雕像? 很棒</b><b>
With the statue behind me? Excellent.</b>

43:46.330 --> 43:48.870
<b>雷曼真的同意申请破产了?</b><b>
Did Lehman actually agree to file?</b>

43:57.760 --> 43:59.260
<b>克里斯 给雷曼打电话</b><b>
Chris, call Lehman.</b>

43:59.340 --> 44:00.920
<b>确保他们马上申请</b><b>
Make sure they file right now.</b>

44:01.630 --> 44:02.680
<b>一定</b><b>
Absolutely.</b>

44:14.980 --> 44:16.860
<b>美国国际集团是个大麻烦</b><b>
AIG's a huge problem.</b>

44:16.940 --> 44:19.650
<b>账目一团乱 不过我现在可以告诉你</b><b>
The books are a mess. But from what I can tell,</b>

44:19.740 --> 44:22.650
<b>世界上一半的银行和这群家伙有关联</b><b>
half the banks in the world are in bed with these guys.</b>

44:22.740 --> 44:24.910
<b>所有做过按揭抵押的银行</b><b>
Everyone who had a piece-of-crap mortgage security</b>

44:24.990 --> 44:28.410
<b>都在美国国际集团为其风险投过保 我是说所有</b><b>
bought insurance on their risk from AIG, and I mean everyone.</b>

44:28.490 --> 44:30.830
<b>他们怎么能让这种事发生?</b><b>
How could they let this happen?</b>

44:30.910 --> 44:34.960
<b>他们肯定是觉得 房地产市场不会崩塌 绝不会</b><b>
They must have figured real estate would never go down, ever.</b>

44:35.710 --> 44:37.630
<b>汉克 雷曼还没申请</b><b>
Hank, Lehman still hasn't filed.</b>

44:40.300 --> 44:43.930
<b>考克斯必须要发布公告了 亚洲股市要开盘了</b><b>
Cox has to make his announcement. Asia's opening.</b>

44:44.010 --> 44:45.180
<b>他和他们谈过了吗?</b><b>
Has he talked to them?</b>

44:45.260 --> 44:47.470
<b>他根本还没打</b><b>
He hasn't even called yet.</b>

44:47.560 --> 44:50.140
<b>我们把巴克莱的事告诉了富尔德 我们说考克斯会打电话给他</b><b>
We told Fuld about Barclays. We said Cox was gonna call.</b>

44:50.220 --> 44:53.390
<b>他就让所有股东坐在那里 不许接电话</b><b>
He's got his entire board sitting there, no call.</b>

44:54.100 --> 44:55.230
<b>考克斯拒不开口</b><b>
Cox is like a deer in the headlights.</b>

44:55.980 --> 44:57.940
<b>混账!</b><b>
Son of a bitch!</b>

45:03.950 --> 45:07.740
<b>你是他们的监管方 马上给雷曼董事会打电话</b><b>
You are their regulator. Call the Lehman board now.</b>

45:07.830 --> 45:10.410
<b>汉克 现在的情况非常复杂...</b><b>
Hank, it's a complicated situation where...</b>

45:10.500 --> 45:12.410
<b>亚洲要开盘了</b><b>
Asia's opening.</b>

45:12.500 --> 45:14.250
<b>他们不公告 市场就完了</b><b>
They don't announce, the market goes in the toilet.</b>

45:14.330 --> 45:17.380
<b>我们必须考虑政府在其中扮演何种角色才比较恰当</b><b>
We have to consider the appropriate role of government here.</b>

45:17.460 --> 45:19.540
<b>我身为证监会主席 能否提议...</b><b>
Can I, as Chairman of SEC, move forward and...</b>

45:19.630 --> 45:22.050
<b>你们就像是不能出面的幕后人</b><b>
You guys are like the gang that can't shoot straight.</b>

45:22.130 --> 45:23.800
<b>这就是你们的工作</b><b>
This is your job.</b>

45:24.800 --> 45:27.970
<b>赶紧去打电话</b><b>
Make the damn phone call.</b>

45:35.270 --> 45:37.020
<b>克里斯 我是迪克·富尔德</b><b>
Chris, this is Dick Fuld.</b>

45:37.110 --> 45:41.780
<b>董事会成员正在开会 大家都到齐了 所有的股东和公司的法律顾问</b><b>
The board is in session. Everyone is here. All the directors and the firm's counsel.</b>

45:41.860 --> 45:45.240
<b>我们明白和巴克莱的谈判已经失败</b><b>
We understand the Barclays deal has imploded.</b>

45:46.700 --> 45:52.410
<b>我们在想你们有没有我们还没想到的解决方案</b><b>
We were hoping you might have some option that we haven't thought of yet.</b>

45:53.040 --> 45:56.460
<b>你知道 市场现在处于一团乱的状态</b><b>
Um, the markets are in turmoil, as you know.</b>

45:57.080 --> 45:59.210
<b>我相信 雷曼兄弟的破产</b><b>
A Lehman bankruptcy will help</b>

45:59.290 --> 46:02.050
<b>有助于消除不稳定性因素 起到稳定市场的作用</b><b>
settle that uncertainty and, we believe, calm the market.</b>

46:02.130 --> 46:04.880
<b>不管是联邦政府还是证监会都同意了</b><b>
Both the Fed and SEC are in agreement about this.</b>

46:04.970 --> 46:08.800
<b>让我... 不好意思 我来说说看看我是不是理解了</b><b>
Let me... I'm sorry, let me see if I understand this.</b>

46:08.890 --> 46:12.680
<b>你是想命令我们使雷曼兄弟破产吗?</b><b>
Are you directing us to put Lehman into bankruptcy?</b>

46:12.770 --> 46:14.560
<b>给我们几分钟</b><b>
Give us a moment.</b>

46:15.980 --> 46:17.730
<b>- 他们静音了  - 这是怎么回事?</b><b>
- He's muted.  - What the hell was that?</b>

46:20.860 --> 46:22.900
<b>让他们去申请破产</b><b>
Tell them to file.</b>

46:22.980 --> 46:26.070
<b>任何在本次会议上的发言会被作为公共记录</b><b>
Everything said in that meeting is or will be public record.</b>

46:26.150 --> 46:28.280
<b>我不能命令一家私人公司申请破产</b><b>
I can't tell a private company to file for bankruptcy.</b>

46:28.360 --> 46:31.530
<b>我没这权利的吧?</b><b>
I don't have that power. Do I?</b>

46:35.960 --> 46:37.040
<b>去做</b><b>
Do it.</b>

46:49.470 --> 46:55.060
<b>董事会需要做出一个决定 提出破产保护的申请</b><b>
The decision to file for bankruptcy protection is one the board needs to make.</b>

46:56.020 --> 47:00.350
<b>这并非政府的决定 但我们相信</b><b>
It is not the government's decision. But we do believe</b>

47:02.730 --> 47:04.690
<b>必须有人来解决问题</b><b>
that the situation should be resolved.</b>

47:04.860 --> 47:07.360
<b>所以你不是在命令我们申请?</b><b>
So you're not directing us to file?</b>

47:07.900 --> 47:11.660
<b>我要说的就这么多了 谢谢</b><b>
I'm not saying anything more than I've just said. Thank you.</b>

47:24.840 --> 47:26.760
<b>投票吧</b><b>
Take the vote.</b>

47:28.420 --> 47:30.680
<b>- 阿克斯先生?  - 同意</b><b>
- Mr. Akers?  - Yes.</b>

47:30.760 --> 47:32.340
<b>克里斯托夫先生?</b><b>
Sir Christopher?</b>

47:34.220 --> 47:35.350
<b>同意</b><b>
Yes.</b>

47:35.430 --> 47:37.350
<b>阿德曼尔·埃文斯呢?</b><b>
Admiral Evans?</b>

47:37.430 --> 47:40.140
<b>很遗憾 我同意</b><b>
I'm sorry, but yes.</b>

47:40.940 --> 47:42.480
<b>富尔德主席呢?</b><b>
Chairman Fuld?</b>

47:45.610 --> 47:46.940
<b>迪克呢?</b><b>
Dick?</b>

47:52.910 --> 47:54.030
<b>同意</b><b>
Yes.</b>

47:57.660 --> 48:00.750
<b>- 赫尔南德斯先生?  - 同意</b><b>
- Mr. Hernandez?  - Yes.</b>

48:02.330 --> 48:05.250
<b>- 阿斯莱尔先生?  - 同意</b><b>
- Mr. Ainslie?  - Yes.</b>

48:06.130 --> 48:08.420
<b>- 贝兰德先生?  - 同意</b><b>
- Mr. Berlind?  - Yes.</b>

48:08.920 --> 48:11.550
<b>- 科拉科斯先生?  - 同意</b><b>
- Mr. Cruikshank?  - Yes.</b>

48:11.630 --> 48:14.890
<b>- 卡夫曼博士?  - 同意</b><b>
- Dr. Kaufman?  - Yes.</b>

48:14.970 --> 48:16.640
<b>- 马克布先生?  - 同意</b><b>
- Mr. Macomber?  - Yes.</b>

48:19.770 --> 48:20.980
<b>是P吗?</b><b>
P?</b>

48:21.890 --> 48:24.480
<b>- 雷曼完蛋了  - 哦 亲爱的</b><b>
- Lehman's gone.  - Oh, honey.</b>

48:24.560 --> 48:26.230
<b>我本该料到英国那边会出问题的</b><b>
I should have known the British were gonna be a problem.</b>

48:26.320 --> 48:28.860
<b>两天前我和他们谈过 那时我应该察觉出言下之意的</b><b>
I spoke to them two days ago. I should have read between the lines.</b>

48:32.240 --> 48:37.410
<b>你不能独自承受一切 这件事涉及了太多人</b><b>
You can't take all this on. There's a lot of other people involved.</b>

48:37.490 --> 48:40.410
<b>是我的问题 因为我是财政部长</b><b>
It's on me. I'm Treasury Secretary</b>

48:40.500 --> 48:42.960
<b>在我的监管下 我国第四大投资银行</b><b>
and the fourth-largest investment bank in the country</b>

48:43.040 --> 48:44.790
<b>倒闭了</b><b>
failed on my watch.</b>

48:45.750 --> 48:47.380
<b>我是说...</b><b>
I mean...</b>

48:50.170 --> 48:52.010
<b>我不知道将来会发生什么</b><b>
I don't know what's gonna happen.</b>

48:54.510 --> 48:56.260
<b>我也想你</b><b>
Miss you, too.</b>

49:00.850 --> 49:05.830
<b>2008年9月15日 周一,早上6:30</b>

49:42.850 --> 49:44.230
<b>哟 出租车!</b><b>
Yo, taxi!</b>

49:47.030 --> 49:48.240
<b>亚洲股市大幅下跌收市</b><b></b>

49:48.330 --> 49:54.240
<b>专家称:"保尔森终于让华尔街变得一文不值"</b><b></b>

49:58.200 --> 50:00.240
<b>吉姆 我现在在市中心</b><b>
Jim, I'm in midtown.</b>

50:01.080 --> 50:02.910
<b>电子指示器在...</b><b>
The ticker is...</b>

50:04.330 --> 50:05.960
<b>我看到的究竟是什么?</b><b>
What the hell am I looking at?</b>

50:06.040 --> 50:08.380
<b>汉克 没事</b><b>
Hank, it's good.</b>

50:13.050 --> 50:15.220
<b>"财政部和联邦储备局</b><b>
"It is oddly reassuring</b>

50:15.300 --> 50:18.010
<b>放弃雷曼兄弟的决定</b><b>
"that the Treasury Department and the Federal Reserve</b>

50:18.090 --> 50:19.510
<b>意想不到地让人感到舒心"</b><b>
let Lehman Brothers fail."</b>

50:19.600 --> 50:21.640
<b>好的 这条 这条</b><b>
Okay, here it is. Here it is.</b>

50:21.720 --> 50:24.020
<b>"政府的介入会被解读成</b><b>
"Government intervention would have been seen</b>

50:24.100 --> 50:27.770
<b>全球金融体系正处于极度动荡中</b><b>
"as a sign of extreme peril in the global financial system</b>

50:27.850 --> 50:30.690
<b>或是联邦管理当局的监管不力的标志</b><b>
"or extreme weakness on the part of federal regulators."</b>

50:30.770 --> 50:33.070
<b>该死的纽约时报</b><b>
The New York fucking Times.</b>

50:33.150 --> 50:36.150
<b>是啊 不仅是他们 每个人都这么说</b><b>
Yeah, and it's not just them. It's everybody.</b>

50:36.240 --> 50:38.610
<b>谢谢 议员 很感激你</b><b>
Thank you, Senator. I appreciate it.</b>

50:39.990 --> 50:42.370
<b>议会很喜欢</b><b>
Congress is liking it.</b>

50:42.450 --> 50:44.200
<b>我倒是不太确定他们是不是真这么高兴</b><b>
I'm not sure they should be so happy about this,</b>

50:44.290 --> 50:47.370
<b>不过他们觉得我们让雷曼退出是对的</b><b>
but they like that we let Lehman go.</b>

50:47.460 --> 50:52.670
<b>你态度强硬 你果敢 在这种时候 人们需要的就是这种态度</b><b>
You stood strong. You've got brass balls. It's what people need at a time like this.</b>

50:53.460 --> 50:54.750
<b>市场反应怎么样?</b><b>
What is the market doing?</b>

50:54.840 --> 50:58.340
<b>欧洲股指只出现小幅下跌 道琼斯指数也小幅下探了3%</b><b>
Europe's only down a little. Dow Jones futures only off 3 %.</b>

50:58.430 --> 51:00.430
<b>那你就得在新闻发布会上强调这点</b><b>
So you need to build on this at the press conference.</b>

51:00.510 --> 51:03.810
<b>你要告诉大家我们已经为雷曼兄弟做了我们能做的一切</b><b>
The story is we did everything we could for Lehman.</b>

51:03.890 --> 51:05.560
<b>- 我们的确做了  - 但是放弃的理由是...</b><b>
- We did.  - And the takeaway is...</b>

51:05.640 --> 51:07.270
<b>没有援助资金了</b><b>
No more bailouts.</b>

51:08.600 --> 51:10.020
<b>部长先生</b><b>
Mr. Secretary.</b>

51:10.100 --> 51:11.810
<b>我们应该如何解读发生在雷曼兄弟身上的事件?</b><b>
How should we read what happened with Lehman?</b>

51:12.020 --> 51:16.570
<b>解读成我认为维护市场的稳定和金融系统的有序</b><b>
Read it as I think it's important to maintain the stability</b>

51:16.650 --> 51:20.240
<b>是至关重要的</b><b>
and orderliness of our financial system,</b>

51:20.320 --> 51:23.780
<b>还有 呃 就是</b><b>
and, um, the</b>

51:26.120 --> 51:28.580
<b>我非常重视道德风险</b><b>
moral hazard is something I don't take lightly.</b>

51:28.660 --> 51:30.830
<b>- 保尔森先生  - 部长 先生</b><b>
- Mr. Paulson.  - Mr. Secretary, sir.</b>

51:30.920 --> 51:34.420
<b>你认为现在的银行体系是否健全?</b><b>
How do you see the health of the banking system today?</b>

51:34.500 --> 51:36.090
<b>当今市场的运行</b><b>
The way the markets are performing today,</b>

51:36.170 --> 51:38.590
<b>是对于验证在极端情况下</b><b>
it's a testament to how the financial industry has come together</b>

51:38.670 --> 51:41.470
<b>整个金融行业是否能同心协力渡过难关的考验</b><b>
in an extraordinary set of circumstances.</b>

51:41.550 --> 51:45.760
<b>美国民众应该对金融系统的稳健和韧性</b><b>
The American people can remain confident in the soundness and the resilience</b>

51:45.850 --> 51:49.430
<b>持乐观态度 谢谢各位</b><b>
of the financial system. Thank you all.</b>

51:49.520 --> 51:52.520
<b>- 部长大人  - 保尔森先生</b><b>
- Mr. Secretary.  - Mr. Paulson.</b>

51:53.150 --> 51:54.190
<b>怎么了?</b><b>
What?</b>

51:54.270 --> 51:57.320
<b>道琼斯大幅下挫 已经下跌了400点了</b><b>
Dow is falling off a cliff. Four hundred points already.</b>

51:57.400 --> 51:59.440
<b>整个信贷市场也处于冻结状态</b><b>
And the credit markets are frozen.</b>

51:59.530 --> 52:02.110
<b>高盛和摩根斯坦利收到大量撤资申请</b><b>
Goldman and Morgan Stanley are getting slammed by withdrawals.</b>

52:02.200 --> 52:04.280
<b>雷曼事件正在危及他们</b><b>
The Lehman thing's killing them.</b>

52:06.040 --> 52:10.210
<b>我得和总统谈谈我们该如何控制损失</b><b>
I should talk to the President about how we'll contain the damage.</b>

52:10.370 --> 52:12.830
<b>在你找总统谈话之前</b><b>
Before you speak to the President,</b>

52:13.540 --> 52:14.790
<b>我们还有个麻烦需要解决</b><b>
we've got another problem.</b>

52:16.630 --> 52:17.960
<b>是美国国际集团</b><b>
AIG.</b>

52:18.300 --> 52:22.010
<b>盖特纳先生正在同美国国际集团探讨由企业主导的解决方案</b><b>
Mr. Geithner is working with AIG on a private-sector solution</b>

52:22.090 --> 52:26.760
<b>部长正非常谨慎地跟进他们的进展</b><b>
and the Secretary is monitoring their progress very carefully.</b>

52:26.850 --> 52:30.850
<b>他与国会领导者们也保持密切联系...</b><b>
He's in close contact with the Congressional leadership, most...</b>

52:30.940 --> 52:32.810
<b>白宫希望我们对美国国际集团的情况做简要汇报</b><b>
White House wants a briefing on AIG.</b>

52:32.900 --> 52:36.270
<b>你知道的比我们多 我们有的信息 你也有</b><b>
You're more informed about that than we are. We've got the same information you do.</b>

52:36.400 --> 52:39.320
<b>不 我们并不认为雷曼兄弟破产</b><b>
No, we don't believe that Lehman's bankruptcy</b>

52:39.400 --> 52:41.440
<b>足以整垮整个华尔街</b><b>
is taking down all of Wall Street.</b>

52:41.530 --> 52:42.820
<b>好吧 那你怎么解释...</b><b>
Okay, but how do you explain...</b>

52:42.910 --> 52:47.910
<b>美国国际集团的情况恶化的原因在于...</b><b>
The AIG situation may have been, you know, exacerbated by the...</b>

52:47.990 --> 52:49.740
<b>还有巴尼·弗兰克的办公室</b><b>
And Barney Frank's office.</b>

52:51.750 --> 52:53.620
<b>- 你好  - 突然发生?</b><b>
- Yeah.  - A surprise?</b>

52:54.540 --> 52:56.040
<b>不 美国国际集团已经挣扎了...</b><b>
No, AIG has been struggling...</b>

52:56.130 --> 52:59.130
<b>你们这帮人怎么没在6个月前阻止他们?</b><b>
Why didn't you guys head off this situation six months ago?</b>

52:59.510 --> 53:03.090
<b>因为我们没有魔杖 Doug</b><b>
Because the requisite magic wand wasn't available, Doug.</b>

53:03.340 --> 53:06.720
<b>如果我们找到了 我们会在第一时间通知你</b><b>
But if we do find one, you will be among the very first to know.</b>

53:08.430 --> 53:10.430
<b>布兰克费恩在四号线 紧急</b><b>
Blankfein on four, urgent.</b>

53:10.520 --> 53:11.930
<b>我得走了</b><b>
I have to go.</b>

53:13.190 --> 53:14.230
<b>嗨 劳埃德</b><b>
Hey, Lloyd.</b>

53:14.310 --> 53:16.690
<b>这该死的英国破产管理人</b><b>
The goddamn British bankruptcy administrator</b>

53:16.770 --> 53:19.110
<b>把所有雷曼客户的资产都冻结了</b><b>
froze all of Lehman's customer accounts.</b>

53:19.190 --> 53:21.530
<b>在你下决定之前你没有和他们协商好吗?</b><b>
You didn't square this with the British before you did it?</b>

53:21.610 --> 53:23.070
<b>盖特纳 5号线</b><b>
Geithner on five.</b>

53:23.150 --> 53:26.700
<b>人们陷入了恐慌 他们拿不到钱</b><b>
People are freaking out. They can't get their money.</b>

53:27.490 --> 53:29.530
<b>不是投资者们 是客户们</b><b>
Not investors, clients.</b>

53:29.620 --> 53:32.160
<b>如果消费者觉得他们的钱放在雷曼那儿不安全</b><b>
If customers think their money wasn't safe with Lehman,</b>

53:32.250 --> 53:33.790
<b>他们也不会相信我们</b><b>
they're not gonna trust us either.</b>

53:33.870 --> 53:37.000
<b>没人愿意和我们做生意</b><b>
No one will do business with us.</b>

53:37.080 --> 53:39.000
<b>你得等我一下</b><b>
You're gonna have to hang on.</b>

53:39.090 --> 53:40.130
<b>蒂姆啊</b><b>
Tim.</b>

53:40.340 --> 53:42.880
<b>丹和穆迪投资评级机构通话了 他们今晚要下调对美国国际集团的评级</b><b>
Dan spoke to Moody's. They're downgrading AIG tonight.</b>

53:42.970 --> 53:46.090
<b>虽说这事儿迟早会发生 但雷曼事件加速了下调的进程</b><b>
Would have happened anyway, but Lehman put the whole thing into hyperdrive.</b>

53:46.180 --> 53:47.720
<b>会降到哪一级?</b><b>
How far down are they?</b>

53:47.800 --> 53:49.300
<b>法国财政部长 6号线</b><b>
French Finance Minister on six.</b>

53:49.390 --> 53:51.010
<b>他们不知道</b><b>
They don't know.</b>

53:52.140 --> 53:53.930
<b>我们在努力挽救</b><b>
We're working on it.</b>

53:54.980 --> 53:56.190
<b>克里斯蒂娜啊</b><b>
Christine.</b>

53:56.270 --> 53:59.730
<b>克里斯蒂娜·拉加</b>

53:56.270 --> 53:59.730
<b>法国财政部长</b>

53:56.270 --> 53:58.060
<b>你怎么能让这事情发生在雷曼身上?</b><b>
How could you let this happen with Lehman?</b>

53:58.480 --> 53:59.730
<b>你到底怎么想的?</b><b>
What on earth were you thinking?</b>

53:59.820 --> 54:02.530
<b>我们已做了我们该做的一切 克里斯蒂娜</b><b>
We did everything we could, Christine.</b>

54:02.610 --> 54:06.700
<b>你默许了雷曼破产 汉克 这大错特错</b><b>
You allowed it to fail, Hank. It was a horrifying mistake.</b>

54:06.780 --> 54:09.280
<b>这会给整个欧洲带来灾难性的结果</b><b>
It is having catastrophic consequences all over Europe.</b>

54:09.370 --> 54:11.910
<b>美国国际集团的情况会变得更糟</b><b>
And AIG would be even worse.</b>

54:11.990 --> 54:15.620
<b>整个欧洲银行都与美国国际集团往来密切</b><b>
The European banks have tremendous exposure to AIG.</b>

54:15.830 --> 54:18.830
<b>我们希望从你这儿得到保证 你不会让它像雷曼一样破产</b><b>
We need assurance you will not fail to act, as you did with Lehman.</b>

54:18.920 --> 54:21.630
<b>这不仅仅是美国的问题</b><b>
It is not just an American problem.</b>

54:22.840 --> 54:24.010
<b>非常感谢...</b><b>
Thank you so much for...</b>

54:24.340 --> 54:25.380
<b>是约翰·麦克</b><b>
John Mack.</b>

54:27.180 --> 54:28.840
<b>- 约翰  - 约翰 一号线</b><b>
- John.  - John, one.</b>

54:30.800 --> 54:33.430
<b>雷曼的破产正连累着我们</b><b>
The fallout from Lehman is killing us.</b>

54:33.520 --> 54:37.350
<b>做空者都在抛售我们的股票 我们已经跌了10%</b><b>
The short-sellers are all over us. We're down 10 % already.</b>

54:37.440 --> 54:39.730
<b>你们不知道外面情况有多糟</b><b>
You guys have no idea what's going on out here.</b>

54:40.980 --> 54:42.270
<b>你的收入怎么样?</b><b>
How are your earnings?</b>

54:42.360 --> 54:44.780
<b>很好 我们准备周五公布消息</b><b>
Strong. We're gonna announce Friday.</b>

54:44.860 --> 54:45.900
<b>现在就公布</b><b>
Announce now.</b>

54:47.950 --> 54:49.860
<b>好了 劳埃德 不好意思</b><b>
Okay, Lloyd, sorry.</b>

54:50.200 --> 54:53.120
<b>汉克 如果储户们发现他们不能从雷曼的账户上取款</b><b>
Hank, if depositors see they can't get their assets out of Lehman,</b>

54:53.200 --> 54:57.080
<b>接下来就会有大批人从各投资银行撤资</b><b>
the next step is gonna be a massive pullout from all the investment banks.</b>

54:57.160 --> 54:58.580
<b>杰夫·伊梅尔特 通用电气</b><b>
Jeff Immelt from GE.</b>

55:00.170 --> 55:02.460
<b>天呐 伊梅尔特为什么打电话给你?</b><b>
Jesus, what's Immelt calling you for?</b>

55:02.540 --> 55:05.800
<b>我得挂了 Jeff</b><b>
I have to go. Jeff.</b>

55:05.880 --> 55:11.220
<b>杰弗瑞·伊梅尔特</b>

55:05.880 --> 55:11.220
<b>通用电气主席兼首席执行官</b>

55:05.880 --> 55:11.220
<b>世界最大公司</b>

55:05.880 --> 55:07.590
<b>你得知道现在时态变成什么样子</b><b>
You gotta know what's going on out here.</b>

55:08.050 --> 55:11.220
<b>我们每天的营运现金流出现了问题</b><b>
We're having trouble funding our day-to-day operations.</b>

55:11.680 --> 55:14.970
<b>我们的财务部影响其他各个部门</b><b>
Our finance division is infecting the rest of our business.</b>

55:15.060 --> 55:16.560
<b>通用电气?</b><b>
General Electric?</b>

55:16.640 --> 55:19.980
<b>这件事情波及的不仅仅是华尔街的公司</b><b>
This thing is spreading way past Wall Street.</b>

55:20.060 --> 55:22.190
<b>我明白没有人想去碰次级贷款</b><b>
I get that nobody wants to touch mortgages,</b>

55:22.270 --> 55:25.820
<b>但我们要制造飞机 引擎 灯泡</b><b>
but we're making planes and engines, light bulbs.</b>

55:26.490 --> 55:28.190
<b>我们是家健康的企业</b><b>
We're a healthy company.</b>

55:28.280 --> 55:30.990
<b>如果我们不能有充足的日常营运资金来运营公司</b><b>
If we can't finance our day-to-day operations,</b>

55:31.070 --> 55:34.330
<b>那我们在美国所有的业务都有可能无法运作</b><b>
every business in America's gonna be shutting down.</b>

55:43.380 --> 55:45.630
<b>- 美国国际集团股价多少?  - 收盘价2美元</b><b>
- Where's AIG?  - It closed at $2.</b>

55:45.710 --> 55:49.510
<b>蒂姆觉得我们得采取有力行动 本和我都同意了</b><b>
Tim thinks we need to do something big. Ben agrees, and so do I.</b>

55:49.590 --> 55:51.510
<b>我们能做什么? 美国国际集团又不是银行</b><b>
What can we do? AIG's not even a bank.</b>

55:51.590 --> 55:56.510
<b>联邦政府会在非常紧急时期借钱给非银行机构 </b><b>
The Fed can lend to non-banks under unusual and exigent circumstances.</b>

55:56.600 --> 55:59.850
<b>我们考虑接手80%美国国际集团的股份</b><b>
We're thinking of taking over 80% of the company.</b>

56:02.600 --> 56:05.110
<b>汉克 我们不能这么做</b><b>
Hank, we can't.</b>

56:05.190 --> 56:07.900
<b>今天上午我们还向全体公民普及了道德风险观念</b><b>
This morning we were lecturing the entire country on moral hazard.</b>

56:07.990 --> 56:10.860
<b>美国国际集团有抵押品 他们有资产</b><b>
AIG has collateral. They have assets.</b>

56:10.950 --> 56:14.410
<b>雷曼兄弟没有 我们不能借钱给一个无底洞</b><b>
Lehman didn't. We couldn't lend into a hole.</b>

56:14.490 --> 56:15.950
<b>两者情况不同</b><b>
It's not the same story.</b>

56:16.040 --> 56:17.830
<b>没人会在乎这些</b><b>
Nobody's gonna care.</b>

56:17.910 --> 56:21.040
<b>这又是一桩没有监管的注资行为</b><b>
It's another bailout with no legislation.</b>

56:21.120 --> 56:23.000
<b>国会会大做文章 整个国家也会抓狂的</b><b>
The Hill's gonna go crazy. The country's gonna go crazy.</b>

56:23.080 --> 56:26.840
<b>我们早上乘坐的班机是从美国国际集团租赁的</b><b>
The plane that we flew in on this morning, leased from AIG.</b>

56:26.920 --> 56:29.090
<b>在市中心的建设 是美国国际集团承接的</b><b>
Construction downtown, AIG.</b>

56:29.840 --> 56:35.090
<b>寿险 8100万份保单 账面价值1.9兆亿元</b><b>
Life insurance, 81 million policies with a face value of 1.9 trillion,</b>

56:35.180 --> 56:37.890
<b>上百亿的教师退休金 美国国际集团的资产到处都是</b><b>
billions of dollars in teachers' pensions, it's everywhere.</b>

56:37.970 --> 56:40.520
