Goldman and Morgan Stanley are going down now.</b>

01:06:14.260 --> 01:06:15.630
<b>我们今天必须做点什么</b><b>
We gotta do something today.</b>

01:06:15.720 --> 01:06:16.840
<b>比如说?</b><b>
Like what?</b>

01:06:16.930 --> 01:06:19.470
<b>市场不像投行一样 对吗?</b><b>
The market doesn't like investment banks, right?</b>

01:06:19.550 --> 01:06:21.760
<b>所有的商业模型都拿那些钱束手无策 </b><b>
The money's saying "fuck you" to the whole business model.</b>

01:06:21.850 --> 01:06:22.890
<b>是的</b><b>
Yeah.</b>

01:06:22.970 --> 01:06:26.060
<b>是的 那让他们变成商业银行</b><b>
Yeah, so merge them with commercial banks,</b>

01:06:26.140 --> 01:06:28.650
<b>把投行变成普通的由联邦政府监管的商业银行</b><b>
turn them into regular banks regulated by the Fed.</b>

01:06:28.730 --> 01:06:30.150
<b>他们就能动用储户的钱了</b><b>
They can use depositors' cash.</b>

01:06:30.230 --> 01:06:31.860
<b>这样他们就能通过贴现窗口</b><b>
It will give them access to the discount window.</b>

01:06:31.940 --> 01:06:34.990
<b>向政府以较低的利率借款</b><b>
It's cheap government cash.</b>

01:06:35.070 --> 01:06:37.820
<b>- 你想让他们变得更大吗?  - 这也是没办法的办法 汉克</b><b>
- You wanna make them bigger?  - It's a trade-off, Hank.</b>

01:06:37.910 --> 01:06:40.950
<b>好处是他们可以逐渐稳定下来</b><b>
The upside is it'll stabilize them.</b>

01:06:42.370 --> 01:06:44.580
<b>坏处是</b><b>
The downside is,</b>

01:06:45.580 --> 01:06:48.330
<b>对的 他们会变得出奇的庞大</b><b>
yeah, they'll be really fucking big.</b>

01:06:48.420 --> 01:06:50.000
<b>去做吧 蒂姆</b><b>
Do it, Tim.</b>

01:06:52.960 --> 01:06:54.250
<b>快去做</b><b>
Godspeed.</b>

01:07:12.020 --> 01:07:14.190
<b>嗯 给我接布兰克费恩</b><b>
Uh, get me Blankfein.</b>

01:07:16.110 --> 01:07:18.110
<b>劳埃德 打电话给维克拉姆·潘迪特 告诉他你想合并</b><b>
Lloyd, call Vikram Pandit, talk to him about a merger.</b>

01:07:18.200 --> 01:07:20.240
<b>蒂姆 我们正在尽全力想办法</b><b>
Tim, we're looking at all our options.</b>

01:07:20.370 --> 01:07:23.870
<b>你已经走投无路了 劳埃德 你的银行只能这样做</b><b>
You don't have options, Lloyd. There's a run on your bank.</b>

01:07:23.950 --> 01:07:25.580
<b>你需要钱 花旗又有存款</b><b>
You need money. Citi has deposits.</b>

01:07:25.660 --> 01:07:28.330
<b>花旗现在一团糟 你这里有条不紊 打电话给Pandit</b><b>
Citi's a mess, you're organized. Call Pandit.</b>

01:07:37.760 --> 01:07:38.800
<b>怎么了</b><b>
Yeah.</b>

01:07:38.880 --> 01:07:40.840
<b>我希望你可以考虑考虑和摩根斯坦利合并</b><b>
I want you to look at merging with Morgan Stanley.</b>

01:07:40.930 --> 01:07:43.050
<b>什么 你在开玩笑吧? 我刚刚买了贝尔斯登</b><b>
What, are you kidding me? I just bought Bear.</b>

01:07:43.140 --> 01:07:44.510
<b>我们仍然在想办法让它开始好转</b><b>
We're still trying to make that work.</b>

01:07:44.600 --> 01:07:46.390
<b>你没有买贝尔斯登 它几乎算是送你的</b><b>
You didn't buy Bear. You got Bear as a Christmas present.</b>

01:07:46.470 --> 01:07:50.640
<b>市场现在一团糟 杰米 跟约翰·麦克聊聊</b><b>
The market's a fucking disaster, Jamie. Talk to John Mack.</b>

01:07:50.730 --> 01:07:53.610
<b>嘿 盖特纳说我们可以谈谈合并的事情</b><b>
Hey, Geithner says we should talk about a merger.</b>

01:07:53.690 --> 01:07:55.520
<b>- 你想这样做吗?  - 当然不想</b><b>
- You wanna do a deal?  - No.</b>

01:07:55.610 --> 01:07:57.690
<b>那他为什么要让我打给你?</b><b>
Then why the fuck did he tell me to call you?</b>

01:07:57.780 --> 01:07:59.860
<b>我得到命令去帮助你们公司</b><b>
I'm under orders to try and help you.</b>

01:07:59.990 --> 01:08:03.070
<b>你是个王子 杰米 真的是王子</b><b>
You're a prince, Jamie. A real prince.</b>

01:08:07.000 --> 01:08:11.500
<b>很显然 有人认为把我们的公司进行合并是一个不错的方法</b><b>
Apparently, some people seem to think combining our firms would be a good idea.</b>

01:08:11.710 --> 01:08:14.380
<b>我想说我对于这通电话受宠若惊</b><b>
I want you to know I'm flattered by this call.</b>

01:08:14.920 --> 01:08:18.670
<b>维克拉姆 我没有奉承你的意思 相信我</b><b>
Vikram, I'm not trying to flatter you, believe me.</b>

01:08:18.760 --> 01:08:20.260
<b>盖特纳打电话来了</b><b>
Geithner's calling.</b>

01:08:20.340 --> 01:08:22.930
<b>一摊子破事</b><b>
Here comes goddamn eHarmony.</b>

01:08:23.010 --> 01:08:24.970
<b>嘿 猜猜看 杰米一点都不感兴趣</b><b>
Hey, guess what. Jamie's not interested.</b>

01:08:28.140 --> 01:08:29.270
<b>试试Wachovia</b><b>
Do Wachovia.</b>

01:08:29.350 --> 01:08:31.310
<b>他们是闭着眼睛进行抵押贷款买卖的</b><b>
They were writing mortgages with their eyes closed.</b>

01:08:31.390 --> 01:08:33.440
<b>蒂姆 那只是一块垃圾三明治 忘了他吧</b><b>
Tim, it's a shit sandwich. Forget it.</b>

01:08:39.360 --> 01:08:41.280
<b>我在四小时之内是赶不到你那边的</b><b>
I haven't been able to reach you for four hours.</b>

01:08:41.360 --> 01:08:44.780
<b>这在今天这样的日子里肯定是做不到的</b><b>
That is totally fucking unacceptable on a day like today.</b>

01:08:45.030 --> 01:08:48.080
<b>我不得不让我的公司去评估高盛合并事宜</b><b>
I had to run my team through the Goldman proposal.</b>

01:08:48.160 --> 01:08:49.450
<b>没用的</b><b>
It's not gonna work.</b>

01:08:50.330 --> 01:08:52.870
<b>你已经联系好高盛了 却没给我说一声?</b><b>
You passed on Goldman without even talking to me?</b>

01:08:53.040 --> 01:08:55.880
<b>我不需要在我的资产负债表上多出1兆亿的美元</b><b>
I don't need another trillion dollars on my balance sheet.</b>

01:08:59.670 --> 01:09:03.720
<b>下次我打给你的时候 记得接电话</b><b>
Next time I call, pick up.</b>

01:09:05.350 --> 01:09:06.850
<b>去死吧</b><b>
Fucker.</b>

01:09:07.100 --> 01:09:10.470
<b>问题就在于那些不良资产 我们把他们买过来就好了</b><b>
The problem is the toxic assets. Let's just buy them.</b>

01:09:10.560 --> 01:09:12.390
<b>哦 可以称为现金换垃圾</b><b>
Ooh. We'll call it Cash for Trash.</b>

01:09:12.560 --> 01:09:15.060
<b>当市场稳定下来了 我们再把这些垃圾倾销掉</b><b>
When the market stabilizes, we'll unload them.</b>

01:09:15.150 --> 01:09:17.190
<b>希望是这样 财政部能够把这些钱讨回来</b><b>
Hopefully, Treasury will get its money back.</b>

01:09:17.270 --> 01:09:19.730
<b>- 这是破杯计划的一部分吗?  - 基本上是</b><b>
- Is that in the Break the Glass plan?  - Basically.</b>

01:09:19.820 --> 01:09:22.740
<b>我的这份是不是少了几页 有谁能告诉我余下的几页...</b><b>
My copy's missing some pages. Could someone else show me the rest of...</b>

01:09:22.820 --> 01:09:24.490
<b>这个是简洁版</b><b>
It's succinct.</b>

01:09:25.200 --> 01:09:27.660
<b>我们在国会只有一次机会</b><b>
We've got one shot with Congress.</b>

01:09:27.740 --> 01:09:31.290
<b>你觉得国会会根据这三页纸就签署一份法案吗?</b><b>
You want them to write a piece of legislation based on three pages?</b>

01:09:31.370 --> 01:09:32.410
<b>听着 朋友们</b><b>
Look, guys,</b>

01:09:32.790 --> 01:09:35.120
<b>购买不良资产肯定是一个噩梦</b><b>
buying toxic assets is gonna be a nightmare.</b>

01:09:35.210 --> 01:09:36.500
<b>没人知道这些东西到底值几个子</b><b>
Nobody knows what the stuff's worth.</b>

01:09:36.580 --> 01:09:39.340
<b>也许这些不良资产永远都理不清 银行马上就要倒闭了</b><b>
It'll take forever to untangle. These banks are going down now.</b>

01:09:39.420 --> 01:09:40.500
<b>那我们能怎么做?</b><b>
So what do we do?</b>

01:09:40.590 --> 01:09:43.920
<b>你想要让信用市场继续运作 是吗? 你希望银行能够继续放贷?</b><b>
You wanna unfreeze credit, right? You want the banks to lend people money?</b>

01:09:44.010 --> 01:09:46.680
<b>- 这就是我们想要看到的  - 那就给他们钱让他们放贷</b><b>
- That's the goal.  - So give them money to lend.</b>

01:09:49.810 --> 01:09:51.140
<b>资产注入?</b><b>
Capital injections?</b>

01:09:51.220 --> 01:09:52.270
<b>丹 摆脱别说傻话</b><b>
Dan, come on.</b>

01:09:52.350 --> 01:09:53.850
<b>我不相信你竟然说出了那个带 "N" 的字眼</b><b>
I can't believe you're pulling out the "N" word.</b>

01:09:53.940 --> 01:09:55.140
<b>我没有说要将银行国有化</b><b>
I'm not saying nationalize the banks.</b>

01:09:55.230 --> 01:09:58.560
<b>我说的是把有问题的银行隔离开 然后进行注资</b><b>
I'm saying isolate the ones that are really in trouble and make an investment.</b>

01:09:58.650 --> 01:10:01.860
<b>- 这做法不是美国人做的  - 当然也不是共和党人做的</b><b>
- It's un-American.  - It's sure un-Republican.</b>

01:10:01.940 --> 01:10:05.200
<b>你让政府变成了一个股东</b><b>
You'd make the government a stockholder.</b>

01:10:05.280 --> 01:10:08.990
<b>什么 我们是不是需要告诉他们怎么去经营 买哪些卖哪些?</b><b>
What, do we tell them how to manage themselves, what to buy and sell?</b>

01:10:09.080 --> 01:10:11.950
<b>像经营邮局一样经营他们? 是那样就太好了</b><b>
Run them like the post office? 'Cause that works like a dream.</b>

01:10:12.040 --> 01:10:15.960
<b>这只是暂时措施 我们可以是没有投票权的股东</b><b>
We make it temporary. We make ourselves non-voting stockholders.</b>

01:10:16.170 --> 01:10:19.380
<b>你不能捧着一叠叠的钞票送到银行里</b><b>
You can't just hand the banks massive piles of cash.</b>

01:10:19.460 --> 01:10:21.040
<b>没人会去理会这些的</b><b>
Nobody's gonna go for it.</b>

01:10:21.130 --> 01:10:25.010
<b>对于共和党来说这是资产国有化 对于民主党来说这就是救助</b><b>
To the Republicans it's nationalization. To the Democrats it's a bailout.</b>

01:10:25.090 --> 01:10:26.680
<b>而且银行会很生气的</b><b>
And the banks are gonna go ballistic.</b>

01:10:26.840 --> 01:10:31.810
<b>抱歉 丹 这是不可能的 很欣赏你的创造性思维</b><b>
Sorry, Dan, not gonna happen. Kudos for out-of-the-box thinking.</b>

01:10:31.890 --> 01:10:35.310
<b>尼尔 如果我们实行你的计划购买那些资产</b><b>
Neel, if we go with your plan to buy the assets,</b>

01:10:35.390 --> 01:10:36.560
<b>我们会花多少钱?</b><b>
how much is it gonna cost?</b>

01:10:36.640 --> 01:10:38.020
<b>那是不可能的</b><b>
It won't work.</b>

01:10:38.100 --> 01:10:41.610
<b>听着 计划只有3页长 而且很空洞</b><b>
Look, the plan is three pages long, totally vague.</b>

01:10:41.690 --> 01:10:46.070
<b>如果购买资产没有用的话 我们会用你的国有化计划 好吗?</b><b>
If buying the assets doesn't work, we'll nationalize the banks for you, okay?</b>

01:10:46.320 --> 01:10:50.120
<b>- 要多少钱?  - 保守估计 需要一万亿</b><b>
- How much?  - To be safe, maybe a trillion.</b>

01:10:50.830 --> 01:10:53.370
<b>国会是不会批准一万亿的法案的 永远不会</b><b>
The Congress will never do a trillion, never.</b>

01:10:53.540 --> 01:10:57.040
<b>有11万亿美元的住房抵押债券</b><b>
There's $11 trillion in residential mortgages.</b>

01:10:57.120 --> 01:11:02.420
<b>还有三万亿的商业债券 一共是十四万亿 对吗?</b><b>
There's three trillion in commercial mortgages. That's 14 trillion, right?</b>

01:11:02.500 --> 01:11:05.550
<b>别忘了5%的违约率</b><b>
You gotta figure about 5% default rate.</b>

01:11:06.510 --> 01:11:09.130
<b>14万亿的5%是</b><b>
5 % of 14 trillion is</b>

01:11:10.260 --> 01:11:12.220
<b>七千万美元</b><b>
$700 billion.</b>

01:11:15.520 --> 01:11:17.770
<b>这也比一万亿要好</b><b>
It's better than a trillion.</b>

01:11:21.440 --> 01:11:24.730
<b>让法案通过的唯一方法只能是吓得他们屁滚尿流</b><b>
The only way to get this done is to just scare them shitless.</b>

01:11:24.820 --> 01:11:28.030
<b>这很简单 我自己都吓傻了</b><b>
That should be easy. I'm scared shitless myself.</b>

01:11:28.020 --> 01:11:31.030
<b>2008年9月18日 星期四,雷曼兄弟破产后第三天</b>

01:11:40.040 --> 01:11:43.380
<b>巴尼·弗兰克</b>

01:11:40.040 --> 01:11:43.380
<b>(马萨诸塞州代表)</b>

01:11:40.040 --> 01:11:43.380
<b>众议院金融管理委员会主席</b>

01:11:41.040 --> 01:11:43.380
<b>问题资产剥离计划?</b><b>
Troubled Asset Relief Program?</b>

01:11:43.460 --> 01:11:44.880
<b>我们称他为TARP </b><b>
TARP, we're calling it.</b>

01:11:44.960 --> 01:11:48.260
<b>这只是你们的草案?</b><b>
This is your draft of the bill?</b>

01:11:48.340 --> 01:11:50.720
<b>这只是一个修订本 肯定的</b><b>
Subject to revision, certainly.</b>

01:11:53.010 --> 01:11:56.010
<b>克里斯·杜德</b>

01:11:53.010 --> 01:11:56.010
<b>(康乃迪克州代表)</b>

01:11:53.010 --> 01:11:56.010
<b>参议院银行委员会主席</b>

01:11:54.010 --> 01:11:56.010
<b>我只拿到了三页纸 我是不是漏掉了什么?</b><b>
I've only got three pages here. Am I missing something?</b>

01:11:56.640 --> 01:11:58.430
<b>没有</b><b>
No.</b>

01:11:58.530 --> 01:12:02.600
<b>理查德·谢尔比</b>

01:11:58.530 --> 01:12:02.600
<b>(阿拉巴马州代表)</b>

01:11:58.530 --> 01:12:02.600
<b>参议院银行委员会副主席</b>

01:11:59.730 --> 01:12:02.600
<b>你在着急寻找的只是一张大额的空白支票</b><b>
You're just looking for a big blank check in a hurry.</b>

01:12:02.900 --> 01:12:06.320
<b>这都是为了银行 你也不想</b><b>
It's all for the banks. You don't want a penny</b>

01:12:06.400 --> 01:12:08.610
<b>让布什总统失去他的总统位置</b><b>
for the average Joe that's about to lose his house?</b>

01:12:08.700 --> 01:12:10.780
<b>整件事完全没有任何监管</b><b>
There's not a scrap of oversight built into this,</b>

01:12:10.860 --> 01:12:13.620
<b>钱没有给银行 也没有给你 只是为了解决这个情况</b><b>
not for the banks or for you, for that matter.</b>

01:12:13.700 --> 01:12:18.450
<b>你希望我们简简单单的拿出7000万来相信你?</b><b>
You want us to simply hand over $700 billion and trust you?</b>

01:12:18.540 --> 01:12:21.550
<b>南希·佩洛西</b>

01:12:18.540 --> 01:12:21.550
<b>(加利福尼亚州代表)</b>

01:12:18.540 --> 01:12:21.550
<b>众议院发言人</b>

01:12:18.540 --> 01:12:20.750
<b>你怎么可能没有想到我们的反应?</b><b>
How is it possible you didn't see this coming?</b>

01:12:21.370 --> 01:12:23.460
<b>如果你们想让我再说一遍的话 我没有问题</b><b>
If you wanna rewind the tape, we can do that.</b>

01:12:23.540 --> 01:12:26.800
<b>但是现在 最重要的是我们没时间了</b><b>
But right now, the one thing we don't have is time.</b>

01:12:27.420 --> 01:12:29.510
<b>我们今晚需要一个决议来稳定市场</b><b>
We need an announcement tonight to calm the market.</b>

01:12:29.590 --> 01:12:31.220
<b>我们需要法案在下周通过</b><b>
We need legislation next week.</b>

01:12:34.970 --> 01:12:38.770
<b>我学术研究的内容只有一个</b><b>
I spent my entire academic career</b>

01:12:39.770 --> 01:12:42.230
<b>就是大萧条</b><b>
studying the Great Depression.</b>

01:12:44.940 --> 01:12:48.940
<b>大萧条的起因是因为股票市场的崩盘</b><b>
The Depression may have started because of a stock market crash,</b>

01:12:49.030 --> 01:12:53.700
<b>但是打击到实体经济的是信用体系的瓦解</b><b>
but what hit the general economy was a disruption of credit,</b>

01:12:54.120 --> 01:12:58.700
<b>普通群众无法借钱去做任何事 没法卖房子</b><b>
average citizens unable to borrow money to do anything, to buy a home,</b>

01:12:58.790 --> 01:13:01.620
<b>没法做生意 没法进货</b><b>
start a business, stock their shelves.</b>

01:13:03.170 --> 01:13:06.330
<b>信用是建立现在经济的基础</b><b>
Credit has the ability to build a modern economy,</b>

01:13:06.460 --> 01:13:11.050
<b>但是信用缺乏也可以毁掉经济 迅雷不及掩耳的毁灭</b><b>
but lack of credit has the power to destroy it, swiftly and absolutely.</b>

01:13:13.130 --> 01:13:19.060
<b>如果我们不能做出明确的决断 我们将会重演上世纪30年代的大萧条</b><b>
If we do not act boldly and immediately, we will replay the Depression of the 1930s,</b>

01:13:19.140 --> 01:13:23.980
<b>只是这次情况会更糟 更糟</b><b>
only this time it will be far, far worse.</b>

01:13:27.320 --> 01:13:31.900
<b>如果我们现在不做这些 我们的经济在周一就完了</b><b>
We don't do this now, we won't have an economy on Monday.</b>

01:13:40.330 --> 01:13:41.660
<b>盖特纳的电话</b><b>
Geithner.</b>

01:13:46.670 --> 01:13:48.500
<b>我们把议案交到国会了</b><b>
We took the proposal down to Congress.</b>

01:13:48.590 --> 01:13:49.750
<b>他们会通过吗?</b><b>
Are they gonna go for it?</b>

01:13:49.840 --> 01:13:51.550
<b>他们不喜欢那么短的议案</b><b>
They didn't like the fact that it was short.</b>

01:13:52.050 --> 01:13:53.300
<b>我想简单明了可以加分的</b><b>
I thought concise was a plus.</b>

01:13:53.380 --> 01:13:56.760
<b>他们觉得这样太轻薄或者太傲慢或者别的什么</b><b>
They thought it was flimsy or arrogant or something.</b>

01:13:56.840 --> 01:13:59.680
<b>我不知道他们怎么想 但是他们不会通过的</b><b>
I don't know what they think. They couldn't get past it.</b>

01:13:59.760 --> 01:14:02.100
<b>市场已经无法控制了 他们否决这份议案</b><b>
The market's in a death spiral. They're gonna sink the bill</b>

01:14:02.180 --> 01:14:03.930
<b>因为这份议案太短了?</b><b>
because the proposal is too fucking short?</b>

01:14:04.020 --> 01:14:07.560
<b>他们正在研究 他们会把他弄得长一点</b><b>
They're working on it. They're gonna make it longer,</b>

01:14:07.650 --> 01:14:09.520
<b>加入一些其他东西</b><b>
among other things.</b>

01:14:10.610 --> 01:14:13.940
<b>好吧 告诉我你已经有进展了</b><b>
Look, just tell me you got something.</b>

01:14:16.990 --> 01:14:19.950
<b>不 不 我一点进展也没有</b><b>
No. No, we're nowhere.</b>

01:14:20.030 --> 01:14:21.540
<b>还有谁可以帮助摩根斯坦利?</b><b>
Who's left for Morgan Stanley?</b>

01:14:22.370 --> 01:14:25.790
<b>中国投资有限公司</b><b>
China Investment Corporation.</b>

01:14:27.540 --> 01:14:29.040
<b>嗯 或者是三菱集团</b><b>
Uh, maybe Mitsubishi.</b>

01:14:29.130 --> 01:14:31.710
<b>不 日本人是不会做这笔生意的</b><b>
No, the Japanese will never do this deal.</b>

01:14:32.170 --> 01:14:33.300
<b>那高盛有什么进展?</b><b>
How about Goldman?</b>

01:14:33.460 --> 01:14:36.130
<b>高盛找到了联银行 但是他们被拒绝了</b><b>
Goldman's looking at Wachovia, but they're so fucked,</b>

01:14:36.220 --> 01:14:38.640
<b>就连约翰·麦克都不屑一顾</b><b>
even John Mack turned up his nose.</b>

01:14:41.430 --> 01:14:42.930
<b>你必须让议案通过</b><b>
You gotta get that bill passed.</b>

01:14:43.020 --> 01:14:47.560
<b>- 我在努力了  - 那就再努力一点 拜托了</b><b>
- I'm pushing.  - Well, push harder. Please.</b>

01:14:50.650 --> 01:14:53.280
<b>这不会有用的 汉克</b><b>
This isn't working, Hank.</b>

01:15:07.670 --> 01:15:09.250
<b>汉克 怎么了?</b><b>
Hank?</b>

01:15:09.380 --> 01:15:11.500
<b>能让我单独待一会儿吗?</b><b>
Could you excuse me a moment?</b>

01:15:33.150 --> 01:15:37.860
<b>2008年9月21日 雷曼兄弟破产后第六天</b>

01:15:33.150 --> 01:15:37.860
<b>哦 我的上帝呀 高先生 高先生</b><b>
Oh, my God. Gao, Gao.</b>

01:15:37.950 --> 01:15:41.410
<b>对于这件事我很抱歉 但是我们无能为力</b><b>
I am so sorry about this. There's nothing we can do.</b>

01:15:41.490 --> 01:15:45.330
<b>这里是纽约 你知道 我们很高兴我们还能在扬基体育馆买一杯啤酒</b><b>
It's New York, you know. We're lucky we can still buy a beer at Yankee Stadium.</b>

01:15:45.410 --> 01:15:48.160
<b>别担心 反正我迟早都会退出的</b><b>
Don't worry about it. I should quit anyway.</b>

01:15:48.580 --> 01:15:50.960
<b>当你准备好了 我们就进去</b><b>
When you're ready, we'll be inside.</b>

01:15:54.380 --> 01:15:56.050
<b>有什么进展吗?</b><b>
Is there any movement there?</b>

01:15:56.130 --> 01:16:00.630
<b>他们给了一个低的离谱的价格 我假装我没听见</b><b>
They made an extremely low opening offer. I pretended I didn't hear it.</b>

01:16:00.800 --> 01:16:04.970
<b>如果摩根斯坦利的问题没有解决 那市场就不能在周一开市</b><b>
The markets can't open Monday without a resolution of Morgan Stanley.</b>

01:16:05.140 --> 01:16:07.470
<b>我们真的很需要你做一个决定</b><b>
We really need you to do a deal.</b>

01:16:07.640 --> 01:16:09.890
<b>- 你打电话给杰米  - 我打过杰米了</b><b>
- You need to call Jamie.  - I called Jamie.</b>

01:16:09.980 --> 01:16:12.150
<b>他对我们没兴趣 难度太大了</b><b>
He doesn't want us. There's too much overlap.</b>

01:16:12.230 --> 01:16:13.560
<b>我们已经跟他说过了 他会同意的</b><b>
We've spoken to him. He'll do it.</b>

01:16:13.770 --> 01:16:16.520
<b>为了什么 为了美元? 我为什么要这么做?</b><b>
For what, a dollar? Why would I do that?</b>

01:16:16.610 --> 01:16:19.650
<b>我这里还有中投和三菱集团求着要我呢</b><b>
I got China Investment and Mitsubishi kicking my tires.</b>

01:16:19.860 --> 01:16:23.200
<b>我知道这些家伙 他们不可能及时作出决定的</b><b>
I know those guys. They're not gonna close a deal in time.</b>

01:16:23.410 --> 01:16:26.410
<b>我们希望你打电话给杰米</b><b>
We want you to call Jamie.</b>

01:16:26.490 --> 01:16:28.620
<b>让我问你个问题</b><b>
Let me ask you a question.</b>

01:16:28.700 --> 01:16:33.500
<b>因为美国国际集团 雷曼和贝尔斯登的事情 已经有3万5千人失业了</b><b>
35,000 jobs just disappeared in this city between AIG, Lehman and Bear.</b>

01:16:33.580 --> 01:16:38.170
<b>如果我们跟杰米达成协议 他会裁掉2万名摩根斯坦利员工</b><b>
We make a deal with Jamie, he'll fire 20,000 Morgan Stanley employees.</b>

01:16:38.260 --> 01:16:40.170
<b>你觉得这是一个好办法吗?</b><b>
You think that's good public policy?</b>

01:16:40.340 --> 01:16:43.680
<b>约翰 我们关注的是整个金融体系的安全</b><b>
John, we are looking at the whole system here.</b>

01:16:43.840 --> 01:16:45.350
<b>中国人走了</b><b>
The Chinese are leaving.</b>

01:16:45.430 --> 01:16:47.180
<b>高先生发现我们还在与三菱集团谈判</b><b>
Gao found out we're also talking to Mitsubishi.</b>

01:16:47.270 --> 01:16:48.930
<b>我要走了</b><b>
I gotta go.</b>

01:16:49.020 --> 01:16:52.600
<b>好的 把黑柳找来 再找一个日语翻译</b><b>
All right, get me Kuroyanagi and a Japanese translator.</b>

01:16:52.690 --> 01:16:54.560
<b>今晚 我们跟三菱要签好约</b><b>
We're closing with Mitsubishi tonight.</b>

01:16:54.650 --> 01:16:55.980
<b>蒂姆·盖特纳又打电话来了</b><b>
Tim Geithner's calling again.</b>

01:16:57.280 --> 01:16:58.730
<b>你就当没听见</b><b>
Cover your ears.</b>

01:16:58.820 --> 01:17:02.530
<b>你告诉? 蒂姆·盖特纳别来烦我了 我在想办法拯救我的公司</b><b>
You tell Tim Geithner to fucking blow me. I'm trying to save my company.</b>

01:17:05.320 --> 01:17:11.040
<b>2008年9月22日 雷曼兄弟破产后第七天</b>

01:17:05.320 --> 01:17:08.200
<b>我要和他见面 但是确保约在在午饭之后</b><b>
Put him on the schedule, but make sure it's after lunch,</b>

01:17:08.290 --> 01:17:11.040
<b>因为之前我还要与玛德琳碰头 而且...</b><b>
because that way I can fit Madeline in beforehand. And...</b>

01:17:12.160 --> 01:17:14.870
<b>摩根刚才与三菱集团达成交易了</b><b>
Morgan just made a deal with Mitsubishi.</b>

01:17:15.250 --> 01:17:18.840
<b>所以我们是唯一一家没有援助的银行了</b><b>
So we're the only bank with our dick still in the wind.</b>

01:17:19.260 --> 01:17:21.720
<b>我再给巴菲特打个电话</b><b>
I'm calling Buffett again.</b>

01:17:26.430 --> 01:17:28.810
<b>爷爷 他们一直在找你 万一是很重要的事怎么办?</b><b>
Grandpa, they keep calling. What if it's important?</b>

01:17:29.060 --> 01:17:31.100
<b>他们总觉得自己很重要</b><b>
They always think it's important.</b>

01:17:34.600 --> 01:17:37.400
<b>好吧 我会快点解决</b><b>
All right, I'll make it fast.</b>

01:17:38.570 --> 01:17:40.480
<b>巴菲特 感谢你回复我 你最近怎么样?</b><b>
Warren, thanks for calling back. How are you?</b>

01:17:40.570 --> 01:17:44.240
<b>挺好 劳埃德 这次我能帮你做什么?</b><b>
Just fine, Lloyd. What can I do for you today?</b>

01:17:44.410 --> 01:17:46.910
<b>我想跟你谈谈关于入股高盛的事情</b><b>
I'd like to talk to you about taking a stake in Goldman Sachs.</b>

01:17:46.990 --> 01:17:49.580
<b>什么价位? 听上去很贵</b><b>
What do you have in mind? Sounds expensive.</b>

01:17:50.450 --> 01:17:51.870
<b>也许不贵</b><b>
Maybe not.</b>

01:17:54.000 --> 01:17:56.710
<b>你最好给我的是好消息</b><b>
You better have good news,</b>

01:17:56.790 --> 01:18:00.590
<b>也许搞定TRAP之前 我就挂了</b><b>
because I might be dead before we finish haggling over TARP.</b>

01:18:01.210 --> 01:18:04.130
<b>巴菲特准备给高盛注资五十亿</b><b>
Buffett's throwing five billion into Goldman.</b>

01:18:06.640 --> 01:18:08.550
<b>我们脱离险境</b><b>
We're off the ledge.</b>

01:18:09.220 --> 01:18:11.220
<b>暂时而已</b><b>
For the moment.</b>

01:18:11.390 --> 01:18:13.850
<b>十月的惊喜来的早了点</b><b>
The October surprise arrived a little early,</b>

01:18:13.930 --> 01:18:16.600
<b>白宫的总统竞争出现了转机</b><b>
with a game-changing jolt to the White House race.</b>

01:18:17.270 --> 01:18:20.980
<b>是该叫做出奇制胜还是孤注一掷</b><b>
Call it a master stroke or a desperate Hail Mary pass,</b>

01:18:21.070 --> 01:18:24.150
<b>麦凯恩宣布他将暂停竞选</b><b>
McCain announced he would suspend his campaign</b>

01:18:24.240 --> 01:18:27.360
<b>并要求推迟星期五的辩论</b><b>
and asked for this Friday's debate to be postponed</b>

01:18:27.450 --> 01:18:30.330
<b>以便他能回到华盛顿集中精力应对金融危机</b><b>
so he can return to Washington to focus on the economic crisis.</b>

01:18:30.410 --> 01:18:36.370
<b>现在是我们团结一致的时机 再次证明华盛顿有能力</b><b>
Now is our chance to come together to prove that Washington is once again</b>

01:18:36.960 --> 01:18:39.460
<b>领导国家</b><b>
capable of leading this country.</b>

01:18:39.540 --> 01:18:42.300
<b>感谢上帝 他回来了</b><b>
Thank God he came back.</b>

01:18:42.630 --> 01:18:46.590
<b>就像大地英豪里的丹尼尔·戴-刘易斯(演员)</b><b>
Like Daniel Day-Lewis in Last of the Mohicans,</b>

01:18:46.680 --> 01:18:49.050
<b>他会拯救我们的!</b><b>
he will find us!</b>

01:18:51.430 --> 01:18:53.310
<b>- 他们要搞砸了  - 发生了什么?</b><b>
- They're blowing it up.  - What happened?</b>

01:18:53.390 --> 01:18:56.480
<b>麦凯恩想趁机介入 挽救局面 但压根不知道怎么下手</b><b>
McCain wanted to swoop in and save the day, but doesn't have any idea how to do it.</b>

01:18:56.560 --> 01:19:00.690
<b>这可是我们认真商量好几天 写了100页的法案</b><b>
It's a 100-page piece of legislation we've been carefully negotiating for days.</b>

01:19:00.770 --> 01:19:02.900
<b>他以为我们就坐着这玩扔纸团?</b><b>
What, did he think they were gonna sit around and spitball?</b>

01:19:02.980 --> 01:19:04.820
<b>是的 当麦凯恩到这</b><b>
Yeah, when McCain got here</b>

01:19:04.900 --> 01:19:08.530
<b>并且发现这事情已经基本解决完了 他就愤怒了</b><b>
and found out that the deal was basically done, he went apeshit.</b>

01:19:08.610 --> 01:19:11.910
<b>共和党没跟上进度 他们想重新来一遍</b><b>
The Republicans fell in behind their guy. They wanna start all over again.</b>

01:19:11.990 --> 01:19:13.910
<b>民主党发飙 共和党想插进来</b><b>
Democrats flipped out. Republicans dug in.</b>

01:19:14.330 --> 01:19:16.250
<b>- 乱七八糟  - 乱七八糟</b><b>
- Clusterfuck.  - Clusterfuck.</b>

01:19:16.830 --> 01:19:19.580
<b>- 汉克在哪?  - 还在跟麦凯恩说话</b><b>
- Where's Hank?  - Still talking to McCain.</b>

01:19:20.040 --> 01:19:22.340
<b>如果你或者任何其他人做了任何事</b><b>
If you or anyone else does anything</b>

01:19:22.420 --> 01:19:26.420
<b>导致新一轮的大萧条 可别赖在我身上</b><b>
that causes the next depression, it is not gonna be on me.</b>

01:19:26.510 --> 01:19:27.760
<b>我嘴巴很不严的 参议员</b><b>
I have a big mouth, Senator,</b>

01:19:27.840 --> 01:19:29.380
<b>- 口风很松  - 等等</b><b>
- a very big mouth.  - Hold on...</b>

01:19:29.470 --> 01:19:34.350
<b>他不是在威胁共和党总统候选人吧?</b><b>
He's not threatening the Republican presidential nominee, is he?</b>

01:19:34.430 --> 01:19:37.430
<b>- 必须采取一些行动  - 不 不 抱歉 离开一下</b><b>
- Something's gotta be done.  - No, no. Excuse me, please.</b>

01:19:37.520 --> 01:19:38.850
<b>民主党的人在哪里?</b><b>
Where are the Democrats?</b>

01:19:38.940 --> 01:19:40.690
<b>他们就在走廊那头</b><b>
They're right down this way.</b>

01:19:40.770 --> 01:19:42.190
<b>- 南希在吗?  - 是的 她在</b><b>
- Is Nancy there?  - Yes. Yes, she is.</b>

01:19:42.270 --> 01:19:43.400
<b>谢了</b><b>
Thank you.</b>

01:19:51.740 --> 01:19:53.070
<b>南希啊...</b><b>
Nancy...</b>

01:19:57.410 --> 01:20:01.080
<b>哦 上帝 汉克 我不知道你还是天主教徒</b><b>
Oh, Gee, Hank. I didn't know you were Catholic.</b>

01:20:02.920 --> 01:20:05.300
<b>我请求你 别毁了这个提案 这次会议很糟糕</b><b>
I beg of you, don't blow this up. It was a bad meeting,</b>

01:20:05.380 --> 01:20:07.050
<b>但是我们必须达成共识</b><b>
but we need to get together on this.</b>

01:20:07.130 --> 01:20:08.970
<b>我们不是想破坏这个提案的一方</b><b>
We're not the ones trying to blow it up.</b>

01:20:09.050 --> 01:20:11.260
<b>我只是请求你能支持我们</b><b>
I just ask you to stay with us.</b>

01:20:13.720 --> 01:20:15.180
<b>拜托了</b><b>
Please.</b>

01:20:16.770 --> 01:20:20.230
<b>参议院在今早9点27分开始讨论援助议案</b><b>
The House began debating the rescue bill at 9:27 this morning.</b>

01:20:20.310 --> 01:20:22.940
<b>约在下午1点28分 国会完成最终投票</b><b>
At about 1:28 p.m., Congress did finally act.</b>

01:20:23.020 --> 01:20:25.440
<b>- 票数非常接近  - 我们马上来看一下</b><b>
- This is a squeaker of a vote.  - We are down to it right now.</b>

01:20:25.520 --> 01:20:27.480
<b>似乎赞成票大多来自民主党</b><b>
It looks like the Democrats delivered their caucus</b>

01:20:27.570 --> 01:20:29.820
<b>而目前来看共和党不大赞同此议案</b><b>
and the Republicans so far have not.</b>

01:20:29.900 --> 01:20:32.110
<b>你认为他们会怎样修改议案</b><b>
What do you think they could do to change the bill</b>

01:20:32.200 --> 01:20:33.990
<b>以便赢得共和党的选票?</b><b>
to get a few Republican votes over to the other side?</b>

01:20:34.070 --> 01:20:35.530
<b>如果他们吊死那些华尔街的首席执行官</b><b>
If they hang Wall Street CEOs,</b>

01:20:35.620 --> 01:20:37.200
<b>我想他们也许能得到更多的选票</b><b>
I think that would get a few more votes.</b>

01:20:37.290 --> 01:20:40.660
<b>我不清楚他们具体能做些什么</b><b>
I'm not sure what they could do exactly.</b>

01:20:40.750 --> 01:20:44.580
<b>国会的领导很可能认为</b><b>
It is possible that the leadership of the Congress would conclude</b>

01:20:44.670 --> 01:20:47.340
<b>没有任何解决方法可以得到多数票的支持</b><b>
that there's nothing that can get a majority of support</b>

01:20:47.420 --> 01:20:50.420
<b>就看汉克·保尔森和当局能怎么做了</b><b>
and see what Hank Paulson can do and the administration can do.</b>

01:20:52.340 --> 01:20:53.930
<b>领导们正在协商</b><b>
Leaders are negotiating right now</b>

01:20:54.010 --> 01:20:56.350
<b>谁会拿自己的职位冒险 这就是我所听到的</b><b>
who risks their seat. And that's what I'm hearing.</b>

01:20:56.430 --> 01:20:58.180
<b>如果佩洛西觉得议案不能通过的话</b><b>
Pelosi wouldn't have brought the bill to the floor</b>

01:20:58.270 --> 01:20:59.350
<b>就不会将这个议案提上议程</b><b>
if she didn't think it would pass.</b>

01:20:59.430 --> 01:21:01.850
<b>我不知道结果 查理 我没办法回答</b><b>
I don't know the answer to that, Charlie. I can't answer.</b>

01:21:01.940 --> 01:21:03.060
<b>我正在读刚收到的一封邮件</b><b>
I'm just reading an e-mail that's coming to me.</b>

01:21:03.150 --> 01:21:06.110
<b>我想最后的底线就是他们还得重新筹划</b><b>
I think the bottom line is they gotta go back to the drawing board.</b>

01:21:06.190 --> 01:21:07.770
<b>但他们还有时间这么做吗?</b><b>
Do they have the time, though, to do that?</b>

01:21:07.860 --> 01:21:09.360
<b>看看道琼斯工业平均指数</b><b>
Look at the Dow Jones Industrial Average.</b>

01:21:09.440 --> 01:21:11.150
<b>知道吗 你们将会迎来一个大甩卖</b><b>
You know you're gonna get a sell-off.</b>

01:21:11.240 --> 01:21:14.160
<b>你们 此时此刻 我们只能抓紧救生筏</b><b>
You guys, at this point, we just gotta hold on to the sides of the kayak</b>

01:21:14.240 --> 01:21:15.280
<b>挺过去 因为</b><b>
and ride through this because...</b>

01:21:15.370 --> 01:21:17.240
<b>他们没通过议案</b><b>
They didn't pass it.</b>

01:21:17.330 --> 01:21:20.290
<b>- 他们没通过议案  - 这还不够</b><b>
- They did not pass it.  - It just wasn't enough.</b>

01:21:21.580 --> 01:21:24.580
<b>议案以九票之差 未能获得通过 Bill</b><b>
They're gonna end up being nine votes short, Bill.</b>

01:21:24.670 --> 01:21:25.710
<b>再说一次 Steve</b><b>
Say that again, Steve.</b>

01:21:25.790 --> 01:21:27.710
<b>我认为他们会以九票之差否决这个议案...</b><b>
I think they're gonna end up being nine votes...</b>

01:21:27.800 --> 01:21:29.590
<b>如果他们得到剩下的六票... 还有五票尚未投出</b><b>
If they get all six... Five of the remaining votes,</b>

01:21:29.670 --> 01:21:33.300
<b>现在他们差10票 剩下的五票都支持议案</b><b>
they'll be 10 votes short now, if they get all five remaining.</b>

01:21:33.380 --> 01:21:35.470
<b>票选结果在墙上</b><b>
The writing is on the wall there.</b>

01:21:35.550 --> 01:21:36.840
<b>我们却失望的坐在地板上</b><b>
And we're here down on the floor.</b>

01:21:36.930 --> 01:21:38.220
<b>当然 交易员已经站在那</b><b>
Of course, traders have been standing around.</b>

01:21:38.310 --> 01:21:39.930
<b>看着 我们都三五成群的站着...</b><b>
Look, we're all here in knots...</b>

01:21:44.480 --> 01:21:47.480
<b>媒体在新闻发布室等你</b><b>
The networks are waiting for you in the press room.</b>

01:21:48.360 --> 01:21:49.940
<b>我甚至无法</b><b>
I can't even...</b>

01:22:02.830 --> 01:22:04.330
<b>我们得重头再来</b><b>
We have to go back again.</b>

01:22:05.250 --> 01:22:06.830
<b>他们不能对新议案说不</b><b>
They don't get to say no on this.</b>

01:22:08.250 --> 01:22:09.460
<b>好的</b><b>
Okay.</b>

01:22:09.550 --> 01:22:10.630
<b>白宫方面想跟你会面</b><b>
The White House wants a meeting.</b>

01:22:10.710 --> 01:22:12.630
<b>很好 我们要带着新策略去</b><b>
Good. We'll come up with a new strategy.</b>

01:22:12.720 --> 01:22:15.260
<b>白宫必须给国会施压</b><b>
The White House has to push harder on the Hill.</b>

01:22:15.340 --> 01:22:17.760
<b>同时 我们要想好如何运作资金</b><b>
Meanwhile, we need to keep working on what we do with the money.</b>

01:22:17.850 --> 01:22:19.100
<b>让我们表现的好像议案能通过一样</b><b>
Let's act like this is gonna work.</b>

01:22:19.180 --> 01:22:20.930
<b>这种情况下 我们还是谈谈资本注入吧</b><b>
In that case, let's talk about cash injections.</b>

01:22:21.020 --> 01:22:23.140
<b>- 又来了  - 我们不能把银行国有化</b><b>
- Here we go again.  - We can't nationalize the banks.</b>

01:22:23.230 --> 01:22:24.270
<b>这不是国有化</b><b>
It's not nationalizing...</b>

01:22:24.350 --> 01:22:26.100
<b>这就是为什么日本经济衰退达十年的原因</b><b>
That's how Japan got itself a decade-long recession.</b>

01:22:26.190 --> 01:22:27.190
<b>那就是我们想要的结果吗?</b><b>
Is that where we wanna go?</b>

01:22:29.690 --> 01:22:30.820
<b>我们还有什么别的选择?</b><b>
What else do we have?</b>

01:22:30.940 --> 01:22:32.030
<b>现金换垃圾</b><b>
Cash for Trash.</b>

01:22:32.110 --> 01:22:35.110
<b>购入不良资产依旧是我们的出路</b><b>
Buying toxic assets is still our go-to move.</b>

01:22:35.200 --> 01:22:37.780
<b>好吧 想办法简化方案</b><b>
All right. Find a way to simplify it.</b>

01:22:38.660 --> 01:22:41.450
<b>丹 做个方案出来</b><b>
Dan, work something up.</b>

01:22:41.540 --> 01:22:45.250
<b>让我们看看会是什么情况 讨论一下</b><b>
For discussion purposes, let's see what it would look like.</b>

01:22:55.550 --> 01:22:58.300
<b>针对那些支持7千亿华尔街援助的人而言</b><b>
For those who supported the $700 billion Wall Street bailout,</b>

01:22:58.390 --> 01:23:00.510
<b>这是一次出乎意料的失败</b><b>
it was a surprising and stunning failure</b>

01:23:00.600 --> 01:23:02.890
<b>当众议院投票否决此议案时</b><b>
when the House of Representatives voted to reject it.</b>

01:23:03.020 --> 01:23:05.480
<b>对总统布什而言 被共和党同僚打击</b><b>
It's a stinging defeat for President Bush,</b>

01:23:05.560 --> 01:23:08.230
<b>是一次惨痛的失败</b><b>
delivered at the hands of his fellow Republicans.</b>

01:23:08.810 --> 01:23:13.150
<b>我们提出一个宏大的计划是因为我们面临着严重的问题</b><b>
We put forth a plan that was big because we've got a big problem.</b>

01:23:13.400 --> 01:23:17.240
<b>现实就是我们处在非常紧急的情况下</b><b>
The reality is that we're in an urgent situation.</b>

01:23:17.320 --> 01:23:20.490
<b>并且后果会日益恶化</b><b>
And the consequences will grow worse each day</b>

01:23:20.570 --> 01:23:21.990
<b>如果我们不采取行动</b><b>
if we do not act.</b>

01:23:22.080 --> 01:23:24.410
<b>- 我明白 我一直都在说  - 起草新议案</b><b>
- I know. I keep telling...  - Draft of the new bill.</b>

01:23:24.080 --> 01:23:32.000
<b>两天后</b>

01:23:25.250 --> 01:23:26.620
<b>他们那边有什么进展了吗?</b><b>
Are they having any luck with it?</b>

01:23:26.710 --> 01:23:28.460
<b>白宫认为先向参议院施加压力</b><b>
The White House thinks they got a better shot of pushing it</b>

01:23:28.540 --> 01:23:31.500
<b>效果会更好 希望他们是对的</b><b>
through the Senate side first. Hopefully they're right.</b>

01:23:31.590 --> 01:23:33.380
<b>他们叫我们收手 交给他们处理</b><b>
They asked us to back off and let them handle it.</b>

01:23:33.460 --> 01:23:36.510
<b>所以我在试着收手</b><b>
So I'm trying to back off.</b>

01:23:42.430 --> 01:23:44.430
<b>购买不良资产还是行不通</b><b>
Buying toxic assets isn't gonna work.</b>

01:23:45.270 --> 01:23:47.730
<b>- 为什么行不通?  - 太慢了</b><b>
- Why not?  - It's too slow.</b>

01:23:47.810 --> 01:23:48.850
<b>我想我之前就说过</b><b>
I think I've been saying that.</b>

01:23:48.940 --> 01:23:51.190
<b>好吧 我们知道这会很复杂 但是有多慢</b><b>
Well, we knew it was complicated, but how slow...</b>

01:23:51.270 --> 01:23:53.270
<b>两个月 也许更多</b><b>
Two months, maybe more.</b>

01:23:54.190 --> 01:23:55.940
<b>我们怎么会不知道...</b><b>
How is it possible we didn't know how...</b>

01:23:56.030 --> 01:23:58.950
<b>我没问会要多久 行不?</b><b>
I didn't ask how long it would take, okay?</b>

01:24:00.450 --> 01:24:02.120
<b>有别的建议吗?</b><b>
Can we move on?</b>

01:24:02.780 --> 01:24:06.080
<b>那么也许我们能谈谈资本注入</b><b>
So maybe we can talk about capital injections.</b>

01:24:06.160 --> 01:24:07.830
<b>丹 我们真不能那么做</b><b>
Dan, we really can't.</b>

01:24:07.910 --> 01:24:10.120
<b>我想我们没选择了</b><b>
I think we're gonna have to.</b>

01:24:10.210 --> 01:24:16.130
<b>就算尼尔能加快进程 实际上不大可能</b><b>
Even if Neel could expedite the process, which seems unlikely,</b>

01:24:16.710 --> 01:24:20.840
<b>体系正在崩溃 银行现在就需要钱</b><b>
the system is crumbling. The banks need money now.</b>

01:24:20.930 --> 01:24:24.390
<b>如果注资是稳定整个体系最有效的方式</b><b>
If cash injections are the most efficient way to stabilize them,</b>

01:24:24.470 --> 01:24:27.560
<b>那么我们就不能</b><b>
then we can't back off</b>

01:24:27.640 --> 01:24:32.400
<b>因为我们不愿意成为是要将几家银行变成国有化的人而退却</b><b>
because we're uncomfortable being the men who nationalized a few American banks.</b>

01:24:32.480 --> 01:24:33.810
<b>可以肯定的是 这更快</b><b>
It's faster, that's for sure.</b>

01:24:33.900 --> 01:24:37.940
<b>这能够把我们从险境中拉出来 是的 激活整个系统</b><b>
It will push us back off the precipice, yes, unfreeze the system.</b>

01:24:39.650 --> 01:24:44.280
<b>我们给他们一些钱然后他们贷出去</b><b>
We give them some money and they lend it out.</b>

01:24:49.290 --> 01:24:50.460
<b>议案通过</b><b>
The motion is adopted.</b>

01:24:50.540 --> 01:24:53.080
<b>在否决布什政府的TARP计划之后</b><b>
After rejecting the Bush Administration's TARP plan</b>

01:24:53.170 --> 01:24:56.000
<b>仅过了四天 众议院今日通过了议案</b><b>
only four days ago, the House passed it today.</b>

01:24:56.090 --> 01:24:59.380
<b>现在最大的问题是 投资者是否能从此消息中得到慰藉</b><b>
The big question now, whether investors will take comfort in the news.</b>

01:24:59.470 --> 01:25:03.050
<b>市场指数显示股票仍在大幅下跌</b><b>
Current indicators show the stock market is continuing its free fall.</b>

01:25:22.860 --> 01:25:24.160
<b>喂?</b><b>
Hello?</b>

01:25:24.240 --> 01:25:26.530
<b>巴菲特 我是汉克</b><b>
Warren, it's Hank.</b>

01:25:27.200 --> 01:25:29.830
<b>抱歉 这么晚了</b><b>
I'm sorry. It's late.</b>

01:25:31.000 --> 01:25:32.370
<b>我吵醒你了吗?</b><b>
Am I waking you?</b>

01:25:32.460 --> 01:25:33.960
<b>没 没有</b><b>
No, not at all.</b>

01:25:35.000 --> 01:25:37.080
<b>能帮我出出主意吗?</b><b>
Can I pick your brain for a minute?</b>

01:25:37.170 --> 01:25:39.380
<b>当然 什么情况?</b><b>
Sure. What's the problem?</b>

01:25:40.300 --> 01:25:45.470
<b>怎么样让一家健全的的银行接受资本注入?</b><b>
How do you get a healthy bank to accept a capital injection?</b>

01:26:39.940 --> 01:26:42.780
<b>我不得不大老远从加利福尼亚跑过来</b><b>
I had to drag my ass all the way here from California.</b>

01:26:42.860 --> 01:26:44.320
<b>他们甚至不告诉我为什么要过来</b><b>
They wouldn't even tell me why.</b>

01:26:44.860 --> 01:26:46.110
<b>没人知道这是要干什么吗?</b><b>
Nobody knows what this is about?</b>

01:26:46.950 --> 01:26:48.320
<b>不知道</b><b>
Nope.</b>

01:26:53.830 --> 01:26:55.250
<b>跟杰米谈过了?</b><b>
Talk to Jamie?</b>

01:26:55.330 --> 01:26:57.460
<b>恩 他会没事的</b><b>
Yep. He'll be fine.</b>

01:26:58.000 --> 01:26:59.380
<b>你告诉他接下来要发生什么了吗?</b><b>
Did you tell him what was coming?</b>

01:26:59.460 --> 01:27:01.540
<b>额 我告诉他我们会迫使他接受</b><b>
Uh, did I tell him we're about to make him swallow</b>

01:27:01.630 --> 01:27:04.510
<b>不需要的注资了吗? 没说</b><b>
a capital injection he doesn't need? No.</b>

01:27:05.670 --> 01:27:08.260
<b>我只告诉他 我们需要他的帮助</b><b>
I, uh... I told him we need his help</b>

01:27:08.340 --> 01:27:10.800
<b>并且我非常礼貌的请求他今天不要跟我们作对</b><b>
and I asked him very politely not to fuck with us today.</b>

01:27:12.470 --> 01:27:13.560
<b>他明白了</b><b>
He got it.</b>

01:27:15.890 --> 01:27:16.980
<b>她在这了</b><b>
She's here.</b>

01:27:22.090 --> 01:27:26.080
<b>希拉·贝尔</b>

01:27:22.090 --> 01:27:26.080
<b>美国联邦存款保险公司主席</b>

01:27:22.610 --> 01:27:25.860
<b>绅士们 这能奏效吗?</b><b>
Gentlemen. We think this is gonna work?</b>

01:27:25.940 --> 01:27:28.070
<b>啊 是的 他们会喜欢的</b><b>
Oh, yeah. They're gonna love it.</b>

01:27:50.720 --> 01:27:54.430
<b>我们现在要着眼于美国的实际需求</b><b>
We are of the view that the United States needs</b>

01:27:54.510 --> 01:27:57.640
<b>要采取坚决有力的行动</b><b>
to take strong, decisive action</b>

01:27:59.230 --> 01:28:02.310
<b>以缓解金融体系的压力</b><b>
to arrest the stress in our financial system.</b>

01:28:03.940 --> 01:28:06.530
<b>通过新授权的TARP方案</b><b>
Through our new TARP authority,</b>

01:28:07.030 --> 01:28:11.360
<b>财政部将向这间房间里</b><b>
Treasury will purchase preferred stock</b>

01:28:12.530 --> 01:28:14.830
<b>与会的每家银行 购买优先股</b><b>
in each of the banks represented in this room.</b>

01:28:17.370 --> 01:28:19.910
<b>头五年 年收益为5%</b><b>
That stock will yield 5 % the first five years,</b>

01:28:20.000 --> 01:28:21.500
<b>其后为9%</b><b>
9 % after that.</b>

01:28:22.920 --> 01:28:25.630
<b>我们给你钱 你们借出去</b><b>
We give you money. You lend it out.</b>

01:28:25.710 --> 01:28:30.260
<b>这可以激活信贷 稳定银行 重建信心</b><b>
It will unfreeze credit, stabilize the banks, restore confidence.</b>

01:28:31.220 --> 01:28:34.930
<b>每个人都会因为体系中更多的资金而获益</b><b>
Everyone will be better off with more capital in the system.</b>

01:28:35.010 --> 01:28:38.390
<b>这就是为什么你们九个人</b><b>
And that is why all nine of you</b>

01:28:41.190 --> 01:28:43.560
<b>都要参与这个计划</b><b>
will participate in the program.</b>

01:28:47.400 --> 01:28:48.900
<b>我们中有些人不需要资金</b><b>
Some of us don't need any capital.</b>

01:28:49.070 --> 01:28:50.900
<b>你们都需要</b><b>
You all need capital.</b>

01:28:51.570 --> 01:28:53.990
<b>你们不知道在未来一年里市场会变成什么样</b><b>
You have no idea what the market's gonna look like in a year.</b>

01:28:54.120 --> 01:28:55.780
<b>你也不知道</b><b>
Neither do you.</b>

01:28:56.910 --> 01:29:00.160
<b>我可不是你们这些鼓弄新花样的纽约佬</b><b>
I'm not one of you New York guys with your fancy products.</b>

01:29:00.250 --> 01:29:03.290
<b>为什么我要呆在这房间里商量救助你们?</b><b>
Why am I in this room talking about bailing you out?</b>

01:29:03.380 --> 01:29:06.670
<b>强势银行将为弱势银行买单</b><b>
The stronger banks will serve as cover for the weaker banks.</b>

01:29:06.750 --> 01:29:09.340
<b>如果只有部分银行接受注资 那将成为一种信号</b><b>
If just some of you take it, the money's a signal</b>

01:29:09.420 --> 01:29:12.430
<b>就是 这家银行无法存活 市场将吞噬掉它</b><b>
that a bank is too weak to survive. The market will devour it.</b>

01:29:13.720 --> 01:29:15.140
<b>我们讨论的金额是多少?</b><b>
How much are we talking about?</b>

01:29:15.220 --> 01:29:16.890
<b>1250亿</b><b>
A hundred and twenty-five billion.</b>

01:29:20.430 --> 01:29:22.180
<b>美国银行 150亿</b><b>
Bank of America, 15 billion.</b>

01:29:22.270 --> 01:29:24.900
<b>纽约梅隆银行 30亿</b><b>
Bank of New York Mellon, three billion.</b>

01:29:25.690 --> 01:29:28.110
<b>花旗集团 250亿</b><b>
Citigroup, 25 billion.</b>

01:29:28.940 --> 01:29:31.440
<b>高盛 100亿</b><b>
Goldman Sachs, 10 billion.</b>

01:29:31.950 --> 01:29:34.160
<b>摩根大通 250亿</b><b>
JPMorgan, 25 billion.</b>

01:29:34.820 --> 01:29:36.950
<b>美林证劵 100亿</b><b>
Merrill Lynch, 10 billion.</b>

01:29:37.580 --> 01:29:39.700
<b>摩根斯坦利 100亿</b><b>
Morgan Stanley, 10 billion.</b>

01:29:40.250 --> 01:29:42.290
<b>道富银行 20亿</b><b>
State Street, two billion.</b>

01:29:42.910 --> 01:29:45.250
<b>富国银行 250亿</b><b>
Wells Fargo, 25 billion.</b>

01:29:51.300 --> 01:29:54.840
<b>购买不良资产的那个方案怎么了?</b><b>
What happened to buying toxic assets?</b>

01:29:55.300 --> 01:29:57.760
<b>- 那不是个好主意吗?  - 那样太慢了</b><b>
- Wasn't that the idea?  - It's too slow.</b>

01:29:57.970 --> 01:29:59.850
<b>在这之前体系就会崩溃</b><b>
It'll be dead before we sort it out.</b>

01:29:59.970 --> 01:30:03.350
<b>所以 我们就这么把缰绳交给你了?</b><b>
So, we're just handing the reins over to you?</b>

01:30:03.480 --> 01:30:05.390
<b>这笔交易实际上很不错了</b><b>
The deal's actually pretty good.</b>

01:30:05.480 --> 01:30:07.730
<b>你现在对此不屑一顾 等到我们还是得来援助你的时候</b><b>
You turn your nose up at this now and we have to rescue you later,</b>

01:30:07.810 --> 01:30:09.440
<b>条件可就不这么有吸引力了</b><b>
the terms won't be nearly as attractive.</b>

01:30:09.650 --> 01:30:12.110
<b>这是很便宜的资本 这不是最差的注意</b><b>
It's cheap capital. It's not the worst idea in the world.</b>

01:30:12.320 --> 01:30:14.150
<b>这是针对我们中间那些已经有足够资本的</b><b>
It is for those of us who already have capital.</b>

01:30:14.240 --> 01:30:18.660
<b>我们将成为没投票权的股东 这只是暂时的举措</b><b>
We will be non-voting shareholders. This will be a temporary measure.</b>

01:30:21.540 --> 01:30:23.370
<b>要是我们拒绝参与呢?</b><b>
What if we decline to be involved?</b>

01:30:24.250 --> 01:30:27.000
<b>美国联邦存款保险公司的主席就坐在这里</b><b>
The Chairman of the FDIC is sitting right there.</b>

01:30:27.670 --> 01:30:28.670
<b>明天你就会发现</b><b>
Tomorrow you'll find out</b>

01:30:28.750 --> 01:30:31.000
<b>你并不像你想的那样拥有雄厚资本</b><b>
that you're not as well capitalized as you think you are.</b>

01:30:31.170 --> 01:30:33.210
<b>你们会采取什么样的保障措施</b><b>
What kind of protections can you offer on changes</b>

01:30:33.300 --> 01:30:34.590
<b>针对补偿措施的改变?</b><b>
for compensation policy?</b>

01:30:34.670 --> 01:30:38.260
<b>我的意思是 如果政府要成为共有者</b><b>
I mean, if the government is going to become a part-owner,</b>

01:30:38.350 --> 01:30:42.180
<b>是不是表明将由政府来指定酬金?</b><b>
does that mean that the government is going to dictate compensation?</b>

01:30:42.270 --> 01:30:44.350
<b>此刻你是在问我有关你的奖金问题吗 约翰?</b><b>
Are you asking me about your bonus right now, John?</b>

01:30:44.480 --> 01:30:46.520
<b>我在经营一家公司</b><b>
I'm running a company.</b>

01:30:47.190 --> 01:30:51.110
<b>如果美联储告诉我 我不能向有才能的人提供有竞争力的薪酬</b><b>
If the Fed tells me I can't offer competitive pay for talent,</b>

01:30:51.190 --> 01:30:54.360
<b>你将导致这个国家有史以来最严重的人才流失</b><b>
you're gonna launch the biggest brain drain this country's ever seen.</b>

01:30:54.440 --> 01:30:56.110
<b>这就是你们要经营银行的方式?</b><b>
Is that the way you wanna run the banks?</b>

01:30:56.200 --> 01:30:58.570
<b>在偿还欠款给财政部之前</b><b>
Until the money is repaid to the Treasury,</b>

01:30:58.660 --> 01:31:01.660
<b>会有一些限制扣税和黄金降落伞(公司控制权变动需要给高管进行补偿的协定)的规定</b><b>
there will be some limitations on tax deductions and golden parachutes.</b>

01:31:01.740 --> 01:31:03.580
<b>- 果然  - 我真不明白</b><b>
- Well, there you go.  - I don't really understand</b>

01:31:03.660 --> 01:31:06.910
<b>为什么讨论这个话题还如此严肃</b><b>
why there needs to be so much tension about this.</b>

01:31:07.210 --> 01:31:10.840
<b>这个国家在面临自从大萧条以来最严重的经济危机</b><b>
The country is facing the worst economy since the Great Depression.</b>

01:31:10.920 --> 01:31:16.130
<b>如果金融体系崩溃 你们每个人都会遭殃</b><b>
If the financial system collapses, it will take every one of you down.</b>

01:31:24.680 --> 01:31:26.390
<b>给我文件</b><b>
Give me the papers.</b>

01:31:34.230 --> 01:31:35.570
<b>- 你不能就这么签了  - 哦 为什么不行?</b><b>
- You can't just sign it.  - Oh, no?</b>

01:31:35.650 --> 01:31:39.240
<b>- 没有你的董事会的同意  - 我的董事会24小时都待命</b><b>
- Not without your board.  - My board's on 24-hour notice.</b>

01:31:39.320 --> 01:31:41.700
<b>我想他们会同意的</b><b>
I think they'll go along with it.</b>

01:31:41.780 --> 01:31:45.450
<b>如果他们不同意 那就炒了我</b><b>
And if they don't, they'll fire me.</b>

01:31:52.090 --> 01:31:53.670
<b>其他人呢?</b><b>
Anyone else?</b>

01:31:59.720 --> 01:32:01.590
<b>他们打算签吗?</b><b>
Are they gonna do it?</b>

01:32:02.430 --> 01:32:05.100
<b>他们要联系各自的董事会</b><b>
They're calling their boards.</b>

01:32:05.180 --> 01:32:07.350
<b>- 那是个好信号  - 如果他们同意</b><b>
- That's a good sign.  - If they do go along with this,</b>

01:32:07.430 --> 01:32:09.690
<b>我们需要在宣布注资的同时 公布其他举措</b><b>
we should announce something alongside the injections, uh,</b>

01:32:09.770 --> 01:32:13.020
<b>也许是一个收购房屋贷款抵押的计划</b><b>
maybe a program to buy up mortgages.</b>

01:32:13.110 --> 01:32:14.690
<b>我不想草率的公布些不成熟的计划</b><b>
I'm not rushing out some half-assed plan</b>

01:32:14.770 --> 01:32:16.570
<b>只是为了显示我们做了什么</b><b>
just to make it look like we're doing something.</b>

01:32:16.650 --> 01:32:20.070
<b>或许我们能补充些限制条件 限制这些钱的用途</b><b>
Maybe we just beef up the restrictions on how they spend the money,</b>

01:32:21.910 --> 01:32:23.660
<b>以去除毒瘤</b><b>
something to take the stink off.</b>

01:32:23.740 --> 01:32:26.160
<b>加更多的条件的话 他们就不会答应了</b><b>
Put more restrictions on it, they won't take it.</b>

01:32:31.500 --> 01:32:33.710
<b>今天完成的事情太多了</b><b>
One thing too many for today.</b>

01:32:35.800 --> 01:32:39.050
<b>我们所知道的是他们差点搞垮了全美国的经济</b><b>
They almost bring down the US economy as we know it,</b>

01:32:39.130 --> 01:32:41.550
<b>但是我们却不能限制他们如何使用</b><b>
but we can't put restrictions on how they spend</b>

01:32:41.640 --> 01:32:44.800
